#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""agora: a tiny shared discussion thread for several coding agents reading one codebase.

Participants: user, claude, codex, gemini (Antigravity). Messages live in thread.jsonl (source of truth) and are
rendered to thread.md. Everyone reads the code from a read-only snapshot (code/) of the source folder: for a git
repo its tracked + untracked-not-ignored files plus its history, for a plain folder the files no .gitignore
excludes; never secrets-like files (.env*, *.pem, *.key, id_rsa*, *credentials*, ...).

Workspaces: run agora in a project folder and it uses that folder's workspace (thread, state, snapshot), kept in
$AGORA_DATA, else $XDG_DATA_HOME/agora, else ~/.local/share/agora: one per git repo (or plain folder). Options
before the command: --src DIR (discuss DIR), --no-src (a discussion without code), --dir WS (that workspace;
env AGORA_DIR). Legacy: an agora.json with "src" next to this script keeps that source's workspace here.

Config: agora.json next to this script holds install-wide defaults (agents, models, binaries, limits); the
workspace's own agora.json overrides them and alone holds src-related keys (exclude, project, also, history).
`agora setup` writes both. Env AGORA_SRC and AGORA_EXCLUDE (comma-separated) override.
  exclude  left out of the snapshot: path prefixes (data/, runs/; a trailing / means a directory) or globs
           matching the path or any component (*.log, *.egg-info/); gitignored files are always left out
  project  markdown file with project notes appended to the protocol (default PROJECT.md in the workspace)
  agy      Antigravity CLI binary (default: agy on PATH)
  claude   Claude Code CLI binary (default: claude on PATH, else ~/.local/bin/claude)
  also     {"name": "/path/to/repo", ...}: extra repos the agents may read, snapshotted to also/<name>
  history  put the git history (.git) into the snapshots (default true)
  max_files, max_mb, max_file_mb   snapshot limits (20000 files, 500 MB; files over 20 MB are skipped): over a
           limit the snapshot isn't refreshed
  independent_timeout   seconds before an independent round is revealed with whoever answered (default 1200)
  serve    agents the serve loop runs headlessly (default: all three; drop one whose seat a person runs)
  autoserve  joining the chat (or posting to a served agent) starts `agora serve` in the background if none is
           running (default true; env AGORA_AUTOSERVE=0 turns it off); it exits after idle_exit seconds
           (default 1800) with nothing to do and no chat, wait or post --via attached
  max_turns, max_tokens   session rotation limits (defaults 40 turns, 300000 context tokens)
  claude_model, claude_effort, codex_model, codex_effort, gemini_model   per-agent model and reasoning effort
           (default: each CLI's own default; codex effort medium); env AGORA_CLAUDE_MODEL etc. override

Each headless agent keeps one persistent CLI session (codex thread / Antigravity conversation / Claude Code
session, all on the local logins, no API keys) and is resumed with only the messages it hasn't seen. A fresh
session (full protocol + thread) starts deterministically when there is none, after max_turns turns, past
max_tokens of context, when the protocol or project notes change, after a failed turn, or on `agora reset`.
Context means the latest model call's input, not cumulative usage. On a turn/token cap the old session first writes a
private handoff note (open questions, hypotheses, path:line facts) that goes into the fresh session's prompt.

  agora post -a NAME [-t to1,to2|all] [TEXT... | -f FILE | - (stdin)]
                                         as user in a terminal: posts, then opens the live chat (-q: don't)
  agora [--last N]  (or: agora chat [-t to] [--last N])   join the live chat as user: shows the last N messages, follows
                                         the thread and posts what you type
  agora read [-a NAME] [--new] [--last N] [--json]   --new: only unseen messages for NAME, then mark them seen
  agora wait -a NAME [--timeout S]       block until a message for NAME arrives, print it, mark seen
  agora post --via AGENT [-t to] [--vote a,b [--rounds N]] [--timeout S] [--mode M] [TEXT | -f FILE | -]
                                         an agent speaking for the user: posts as the user, prints the discussion
                                         as it happens and returns once the question is answered (prints the
                                         outcomes and why it stopped); --vote polls every agent
  --mode audit|design|independent        (user posts) a longer structured answer, or an independent round: every
                                         agent answers blind, the answers are revealed together, then cross-checked
  agora decide [--via AGENT] TEXT        record a decision; `agora decisions` lists them (also atop THREAD.md)
  agora skill [--install DIR]            print the agent skill for `post --via` (or write DIR/agora/SKILL.md)
  agora doing -a NAME [--id ID [--bg] [--done]] TEXT   show what NAME is doing in the chat (phase, or one of
                                         several concurrent actions); wait sets it, posting clears it
  agora idle -a NAME                     clear NAME's activity
  agora sync                             refresh the code snapshot from the source folder
  agora setup                            choose excludes, the agents to seat, their models and efforts
  agora where | ls                       this folder's workspace | all workspaces
  agora claude | codex | gemini          run that agent once on the thread and post its reply
  agora serve [--budget N] [--only X]    loop: answer as the serve agents whenever a message is addressed to them
  agora reset [NAME|all]                 drop agent sessions: their next turn starts fresh
  agora status
  agora protocol                         print the protocol (PROTOCOL.md + the project notes) with real paths
  agora intro NAME                       print the starter prompt for a seat you run by hand (SEAT.md)
"""
import argparse, fcntl, json, os, re, shutil, subprocess, sys, tempfile, time

INSTALL = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))   # the program: venv, templates, Codex home, default config
SCRIPT = os.path.realpath(__file__)
VENV = os.path.join(INSTALL, ".venv")  # optional: python -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(VENV, "bin", "python")) and os.path.realpath(sys.prefix) != os.path.realpath(VENV):
    os.execv(os.path.join(VENV, "bin", "python"), [os.path.join(VENV, "bin", "python"), SCRIPT] + sys.argv[1:])
NAMES = ("user", "claude", "codex", "gemini")
AGENTS = ("claude", "codex", "gemini")
WS_KEYS = ("src", "exclude", "project", "also", "history")   # workspace-only config: never inherited from the install
DATA = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("AGORA_DATA") or os.path.join(
    os.environ.get("XDG_DATA_HOME") or os.path.join("~", ".local", "share"), "agora")))
SECRETS = (".env*", "*.pem", "*.key", "*.p12", "*.pfx", "*.keystore", "*.jks", "id_rsa*", "id_dsa*", "id_ecdsa*",
           "id_ed25519*", "*credentials*", ".netrc", ".npmrc", ".pypirc", ".pgpass", ".ssh/", ".aws/", ".gnupg/",
           ".codex-home/", ".claude/")   # always left out of snapshots, at any depth


def _json(p):
    try:
        with open(p) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def git_top(d):
    """The top of the git work tree containing d, or None."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", d, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"], capture_output=True, text=True)
    except OSError:
        return None
    return os.path.realpath(r.stdout.strip()) if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip() else None


def _ws_args():
    """Pop the workspace options (--dir D, --src S, --no-src) that come before the command."""
    out, i, argv = {}, 1, sys.argv
    while i < len(argv) and argv[i].startswith("-"):
        k, eq, v = argv[i].partition("=")
        if k in ("--dir", "--src") and (eq or i + 1 < len(argv)):
            out[k[2:]] = v if eq else argv[i + 1]
            del argv[i:i + (1 if eq else 2)]
        elif k == "--no-src":
            out["no_src"] = True
            del argv[i]
        else:
            i += 2 if k == "--last" and not eq else 1
    return out


def ws_path(key, label):
    """The workspace dir for a source (or source-less folder) key."""
    base = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]+", "_", os.path.basename(label.rstrip(os.sep)) or "root")[:40]
    return os.path.join(DATA, f"{base}-{__import__('hashlib').sha1(key.encode()).hexdigest()[:8]}")


def resolve_ws():
    """(workspace dir, source dir or None, how). The workspace holds the thread, state, snapshots and work dirs;
    each source folder gets its own. Legacy: an agora.json with "src" next to the script keeps the old layout
    (everything in the install dir) for that source."""
    o = _ws_args()
    rest = [x for x in sys.argv[1:] if not x.startswith("-")]
    if rest[:1] == ["ls"] or not rest and {"-h", "--help"} & set(sys.argv[1:]) or rest[:1] == ["skill"]:
        return os.path.join(DATA, ".none"), None, "none"   # needs no workspace: don't create one
    legacy = _json(os.path.join(INSTALL, "agora.json")).get("src")
    legacy = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(legacy)) if legacy else None
    src = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(o["src"])) if o.get("src") else None
    if o.get("src") and o.get("no_src"):
        sys.exit("agora: --src and --no-src exclude each other")
    d = o.get("dir") or os.environ.get("AGORA_DIR")
    cwd = os.path.realpath(os.getcwd())
    if d:
        ws = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(d))
    elif legacy and (src == legacy or not src and not o.get("no_src") and (
            cwd == INSTALL or cwd.startswith(INSTALL + os.sep) or (git_top(cwd) or cwd) == legacy)):
        return INSTALL, legacy, "legacy"
    else:
        ws, p = None, cwd   # inside a workspace already (e.g. an agent's work dir)?
        while not src and not o.get("no_src") and p.startswith(DATA + os.sep):
            if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(p, "workspace.json")):
                ws = p
                break
            p = os.path.dirname(p)
        if not ws:
            if o.get("no_src"):
                ws = ws_path("nosrc:" + cwd, cwd)
            else:
                src = src or git_top(cwd) or cwd
                ws = ws_path(src, src)
    if ws == INSTALL:
        return INSTALL, legacy, "legacy"
    meta_p = os.path.join(ws, "workspace.json")
    meta = _json(meta_p)
    if not meta or src or o.get("no_src"):   # new workspace, or the source given again: record it
        if not meta and not src and not o.get("no_src"):
            src = git_top(cwd) or cwd
        new = {"src": None if o.get("no_src") else src, "created": meta.get("created") or time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")}
        if new["src"] != meta.get("src") or not meta:
            check_src(new["src"], ws)
            os.makedirs(ws, exist_ok=True)
            with open(meta_p + ".tmp", "w") as f:
                json.dump(new, f, indent=1)
            os.replace(meta_p + ".tmp", meta_p)
            return ws, new["src"], "new" if not meta else "changed"
    return ws, meta.get("src"), "found"


def check_src(src, ws):
    """Refuse sources that would snapshot agora's own storage or a whole system/home dir."""
    if not src:
        return
    home = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser("~"))
    def inside(a, b):
        return a == b or a.startswith(b.rstrip(os.sep) + os.sep)
    if inside(src, DATA) or inside(DATA, src) or inside(ws, src):
        sys.exit(f"agora: {src} overlaps agora's workspace storage ({DATA}); pick another folder")
    roots = {os.path.abspath(os.sep), "/usr", "/etc", "/var", "/bin", "/sbin", "/lib", "/opt", "/proc", "/sys", "/dev",
             "/boot", "/tmp", "/mnt", "/home", "/Users", "/Volumes", "/media", "/srv", "/root"}
    plain = not git_top(src)
    if src in roots or os.path.splitdrive(src)[1] in ("", os.sep) or plain and src in (home, INSTALL):
        sys.exit(f"agora: refusing to snapshot {src}: too broad. Run agora from a project folder, or use --src DIR "
                 "(or --no-src for a discussion without code)")


WS, SRC0, WS_HOW = resolve_ws()
THREAD, MD, STATE = (os.path.join(WS, x) for x in ("thread.jsonl", "thread.md", "state"))
CODE, CONFIG = os.path.join(WS, "code"), os.path.join(WS, "agora.json")
ICONFIG = os.path.join(INSTALL, "agora.json")   # install-wide defaults (models, binaries, serve, limits)
AGORA = SCRIPT + ("" if WS == INSTALL else " --dir " + (WS if re.fullmatch(r"[\w./~-]+", WS) else json.dumps(WS)))


def load_config():
    """CFG = the install defaults minus workspace-only keys, overlaid with the workspace's own agora.json."""
    global CFG
    inst = _json(ICONFIG)
    CFG = inst if WS == INSTALL else {**{k: v for k, v in inst.items() if k not in WS_KEYS}, **_json(CONFIG)}
    src = os.environ.get("AGORA_SRC") or (CFG.get("src") if WS == INSTALL else SRC0)
    ex = os.environ.get("AGORA_EXCLUDE")
    ex = [x.strip() for x in ex.split(",")] if ex is not None else CFG.get("exclude", [])
    proj = os.path.join(WS, os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("AGORA_PROJECT") or CFG.get("project", "PROJECT.md")))
    agy = os.environ.get("AGORA_AGY") or CFG.get("agy") or shutil.which("agy") or "agy"
    return (os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(src)) if src else None), tuple(x for x in ex if x), proj, os.path.expanduser(agy)


SRC, EXCLUDE, PROJECT, AGY = load_config()
ALSO_DIR = os.path.join(WS, "also")  # extra repos, each snapshotted read-only to also/<name>
ALSO = {k: os.path.expanduser(v) for k, v in (CFG.get("also") or {}).items()}


def also_note():
    """Prompt text naming the extra read-only snapshots, or ''."""
    return ("Also readable (read-only snapshots): " + ", ".join(f"{k} at {os.path.join(ALSO_DIR, k)}" for k in ALSO)
            + ". ") if ALSO else ""
CLAUDE = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("AGORA_CLAUDE") or CFG.get("claude") or shutil.which("claude")
                            or "~/.local/bin/claude")
MAX_TURNS, MAX_TOKENS = int(CFG.get("max_turns", 40)), int(CFG.get("max_tokens", 300_000))
HISTORY = bool(CFG.get("history", True))   # put the repo's git history (.git) in the snapshots
SRC_ID = (("git:" if git_top(SRC) else "dir:") + SRC) if SRC else "none"   # sessions are tied to their source


def winpath(path):
    """Under WSL, (the Windows path of a Linux path, the command prefix to run this script from Windows)."""
    try:
        w = subprocess.run(["wslpath", "-w", path], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout.strip()
    except (OSError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):
        return path, ""
    m = re.match(r"\\\\wsl(?:\.localhost|\$)\\([^\\]+)", w)
    return w, (f"wsl -d {m.group(1)} " if m else "")


def template(fname, **kw):
    with open(os.path.join(INSTALL, fname)) as f:
        s = f.read()
    for k, v in kw.items():
        s = s.replace("{" + k + "}", v)
    return s


def protocol():
    s = template("PROTOCOL.md", agora=AGORA, code=CODE, thread=MD)
    if os.path.exists(PROJECT):
        with open(PROJECT) as f:
            s = s.rstrip() + "\n\n" + f.read()
    return s
BUDGET = 400  # max agent messages since the last user message before Codex stops auto-replying


def author(m):
    return m["from"] + (f" (via {m['via']})" if m.get("via") else "")


def load():
    if not os.path.exists(THREAD):
        return []
    with open(THREAD) as f:
        return [json.loads(l) for l in f if l.strip()]


def tag(m):
    """Header tag: what the message answers, and its round or reply mode ('' for ordinary messages)."""
    re_ = (" ↩ " + ", ".join(f"#{i}" for i in m["re"][-4:])) if m.get("re") else ""
    if m.get("independent"):
        return re_ + f" ◆ independent answer to #{m['independent']}"
    return re_ + {"independent": " ◆ independent", "audit": " ◆ audit", "design": " ◆ design",
                  "decision": " ◆ decision"}.get(m.get("mode"), "")


def wjson(path, obj):
    """Write JSON atomically (a crash leaves the old file or the new one, never half of one)."""
    with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
        json.dump(obj, f)
    os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)


def decisions(msgs):
    """The decisions recorded in the thread (the user's /decide, vote results), oldest first."""
    return [m for m in msgs if m.get("mode") == "decision"]


def decisions_text(msgs):
    ds = decisions(msgs)
    if not ds:
        return ""
    return "## Decisions so far\n\n" + "".join(
        f"- #{m['id']} ({m['ts'][:16]}, {author(m)}): {' '.join(m['text'].split())[:400]}\n" for m in ds) + "\n"


def render(msgs):
    out = ["# Agora thread\n", "Read-only codebase snapshot: `" + CODE + "`. Protocol: `agora protocol`.\n"]
    if decisions(msgs):
        out.append("\n" + decisions_text(msgs))
    for m in msgs:
        out.append(f"\n---\n### #{m['id']} {author(m)} → {', '.join(m['to'])}{tag(m)} · {m['ts']}\n\n{m['text'].rstrip()}\n")
    tmp = MD + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        f.writelines(out)
    os.replace(tmp, MD)


PING = re.compile(r"(?<![\w@])@(" + "|".join(AGENTS) + r"|all)\b", re.I)
MODES = ("short", "audit", "design", "independent", "decision")
INDEP = os.path.join(STATE, "independent")  # <qid>/<agent>.json: answers held until the round is revealed


def post(frm, to, text, via=None, mode=None, extra=None, hold=(), re_=()):
    """via: an agent posting as the user on the user's behalf (agora post --via NAME). mode (user messages):
    the reply shape asked for (audit, design), an independent round, or a decision. extra: more fields for the
    record. re_: ids of the messages this one answers. hold: ids of open independent rounds this agent message
    answers: it is held in each round (not posted) until the round is revealed; returns {"held": qid, ...}."""
    frm = frm.lower()
    if frm not in NAMES:
        sys.exit(f"unknown author {frm!r}; use one of {NAMES}")
    to = [t.strip().lower() for t in (to or "all").split(",") if t.strip()]
    bad = [t for t in to if t not in NAMES + ("all",)]
    if bad:
        sys.exit(f"unknown recipient(s) {bad}")
    text = text.strip()
    if not text:
        sys.exit("empty message")
    if mode and mode not in MODES:
        sys.exit(f"unknown mode {mode!r}; use one of {MODES}")
    hold = [q for q in hold if frm in AGENTS and q in open_rounds()
            and not os.path.exists(os.path.join(INDEP, str(q), frm + ".json"))]
    if hold:
        held = {"from": frm, "to": to, "text": text, "ts": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), "held": hold[0],
                "rounds": hold}
        for q in hold:
            wjson(os.path.join(INDEP, str(q), frm + ".json"), held)
        busy(frm, False)
        return held
    with open(THREAD, "a+") as f:
        fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        f.seek(0)
        n = sum(1 for l in f if l.strip())
        m = {"id": n + 1, "from": frm, "to": to, "ts": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), "text": text}
        if via:
            m["via"] = via
        if mode and mode != "short":
            m["mode"] = mode
        if re_:
            m["re"] = sorted(set(re_))
        m.update(extra or {})
        f.write(json.dumps(m, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
        f.flush()
        fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
    render(load())
    if mode == "independent":   # the round waits for exactly the agents asked when it opened
        d = os.path.join(INDEP, str(m["id"]))
        os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
        wjson(os.path.join(d, "members.json"),
              round_members() if "all" in to else [n for n in AGENTS if n in to or PING_ONE(n).search(text)])
    elif mode == "decision":
        pass   # a record, not a question: nobody is asked to answer it
    elif frm == "user" and to == ["all"] and not PING.search(text):
        take_turns(m["id"])   # a plain question to all: one lead answer (an @agent or @all ping asks everyone)
    if frm != "user":
        busy(frm, False)
        if frm in AGENTS and to and all(t in AGENTS and t != frm for t in to):
            sleep_set(frm, True, why="auto", until_from=to)   # asked another agent: wait for its answer
    return m


def PING_ONE(name):
    return re.compile(r"(?<![\w@])@" + name + r"\b", re.I)


SLEEP = os.path.join(STATE, "sleep")  # <name>.json while an agent sleeps: it skips messages to "all" until pinged


def pinged(m, name):
    """Addressed to name by name (-t name), mentioning @name anywhere in the text, the user mentioning @all, or
    a user question opening an independent round (everyone answers it)."""
    if m["from"] == name:
        return False
    if name in m["to"] or PING_ONE(name).search(m["text"]):
        return True
    return m["from"] == "user" and name in AGENTS and m.get("mode") != "decision" and (
        m.get("mode") == "independent" and "all" in m["to"] or bool(PING_ONE("all").search(m["text"])))


def asleep(name):
    """The sleep record {since, until, why} of a sleeping agent, else None (expired sleeps end by themselves)."""
    p = os.path.join(SLEEP, name + ".json")
    try:
        z = json.load(open(p))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if z.get("until") and time.time() > z["until"]:
        try:
            os.unlink(p)
        except OSError:
            pass
        return None
    return z


def sleep_set(name, on=True, secs=None, why="", until_from=()):
    os.makedirs(SLEEP, exist_ok=True)
    p = os.path.join(SLEEP, name + ".json")
    if not on:
        try:
            os.unlink(p)
        except OSError:
            pass
        return
    with open(p, "w") as f:
        json.dump({"since": time.time(), "until": time.time() + secs if secs else None, "why": why,
                   "from": [x for x in until_from if x != name], "after": len(load())}, f)


def take_turns(mid):
    """A question to all gets one lead answer (agents rotate); the others wait for it, then add only what's new."""
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    p = os.path.join(STATE, "lead")
    try:
        i = int(open(p).read())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        i = -1
    lead = AGENTS[(i + 1) % len(AGENTS)]
    with open(p, "w") as f:
        f.write(str(AGENTS.index(lead)))
    for n in AGENTS:
        if n != lead and not (asleep(n) or {}).get("why") == "user":
            sleep_set(n, True, 900, why="turn", until_from=[lead])   # wakes on the lead's answer, a ping, or after 15 min


def for_me(m, name):
    """Pings always count. A sleeper waiting for someone (WAIT: codex) wakes on that one's next message,
    whoever it is addressed to; otherwise sleepers skip messages to all."""
    if pinged(m, name):
        return True
    z = asleep(name)
    if z and z.get("from") and m["from"] in z["from"] and m["id"] > z.get("after", 0):
        return True
    if z and m["from"] == "user" and "all" in m["to"] and z.get("why") not in ("user", "turn") \
            and m["id"] > z.get("after", 0):
        return True   # the user speaking to everyone wakes agents that went to sleep on their own
    return m["from"] != name and "all" in m["to"] and not z and m.get("mode") != "decision"


def seen(name, val=None):
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    p = os.path.join(STATE, name + ".seen")
    if val is not None:
        with open(p, "w") as f:
            f.write(str(val))
        return val
    try:
        return int(open(p).read())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return 0


def fmt(m):
    return f"### #{m['id']} {author(m)} → {', '.join(m['to'])}{tag(m)} · {m['ts']}\n\n{m['text'].rstrip()}\n"


ROUND_TIMEOUT = float(CFG.get("independent_timeout", 1200))  # an independent round is revealed after this


def open_rounds():
    """Ids of independent rounds whose answers are still held (oldest first)."""
    try:
        return sorted(int(d) for d in os.listdir(INDEP) if d.isdigit()
                      and not os.path.exists(os.path.join(INDEP, d, "revealed")))
    except OSError:
        return []


def round_members():
    """Agents an independent round waits for: the served ones, plus any agent run by hand that was active in the
    last two hours (it updates its seen marker when it reads the thread)."""
    now = time.time()
    def active(n):
        try:
            return now - os.path.getmtime(os.path.join(STATE, n + ".seen")) < 7200
        except OSError:
            return False
    return [n for n in AGENTS if n in AUTO or active(n)]


def members(q):
    """The agents round q waits for, fixed when it opened."""
    try:
        return json.load(open(os.path.join(INDEP, str(q), "members.json")))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return round_members()


def round_status(q):
    """{agent: held record} for round q."""
    d, out = os.path.join(INDEP, str(q)), {}
    for n in AGENTS:
        try:
            out[n] = json.load(open(os.path.join(d, n + ".json")))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass
    return out


def hold_outcome(q, name, **kw):
    """Record that name won't answer round q (it slept or failed), so the round doesn't wait for it."""
    p = os.path.join(INDEP, str(q), name + ".json")
    if os.path.isdir(os.path.dirname(p)) and not os.path.exists(p):
        wjson(p, {"from": name, **kw})


def reveal_due(force=False):
    """Post the held answers of every round that is complete (all members answered, slept or failed) or past
    ROUND_TIMEOUT, together, each addressed to the user and the other agents so they cross-check one another."""
    if not open_rounds():
        return
    os.makedirs(INDEP, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(INDEP, ".lock"), "w") as lk:   # one revealer at a time
        fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        for q in open_rounds():
            _reveal(q, force)


def _reveal(q, force):
    """Idempotent: an answer already in the thread is not posted again, so a crash midway is finished on the next
    call; the round is marked revealed only after every answer is out."""
    held = round_status(q)
    msgs = load()
    qm = next((m for m in msgs if m["id"] == q), None)
    t0 = time.mktime(time.strptime(qm["ts"], "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")) if qm else 0
    if not (force or set(members(q)) <= set(held) or time.time() - t0 > ROUND_TIMEOUT):
        return
    out = {m["from"] for m in msgs if m.get("independent") == q}
    answers = [h for n, h in held.items() if h.get("text")]
    for h in answers:
        if h["from"] in out:
            continue
        others = [n for n in AGENTS if n != h["from"] and n in held and held[n].get("text")]
        post(h["from"], ",".join(["user"] + others), h["text"], extra={"independent": q}, re_=[q])
    open(os.path.join(INDEP, str(q), "revealed"), "w").close()
    missing = [n for n in members(q) if n not in held]
    quiet = [n for n, h in held.items() if not h.get("text")]
    log_turn("reveal", [q], "revealed", note=f"{len(answers)} answers"
             + (f"; no answer from {', '.join(missing)}" if missing else "")
             + (f"; nothing to add: {', '.join(quiet)}" if quiet else ""))


TURNS = os.path.join(STATE, "turns.jsonl")  # one line per agent turn: who, which messages, what came of it


def log_turn(name, ids, outcome, msg=None, note=""):
    """outcome: posted (msg = id), held (independent round), slept (nothing to add), failed, gave up, budget,
    revealed."""
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    with open(TURNS, "a") as f:
        f.write(json.dumps({"t": time.time(), "name": name, "ids": list(ids), "outcome": outcome, "msg": msg,
                            "note": note}) + "\n")


def turns_since(t0):
    try:
        with open(TURNS) as f:
            return [r for r in (json.loads(l) for l in f if l.strip()) if r["t"] >= t0]
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return []


FAIL = os.path.join(STATE, "failed")  # <name>.json after a failed turn: {ids, rc, tries, next}
MAX_TRIES = 4   # the first try and 3 retries (after 1, 2 and 4 min), then the messages are given up


def failure(name, val=None, clear=False):
    p = os.path.join(FAIL, name + ".json")
    if clear:
        try:
            os.unlink(p)
        except OSError:
            pass
        return None
    if val is not None:
        os.makedirs(FAIL, exist_ok=True)
        with open(p, "w") as f:
            json.dump(val, f)
        return val
    try:
        return json.load(open(p))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def note_failure(name, ids, rc):
    """Count a failed turn; retries back off 1, 2, 4 min. Returns the record."""
    f = failure(name) or {"tries": 0}
    tries = f["tries"] + 1
    rec = {"ids": sorted(set(f.get("ids", [])) | set(ids)), "rc": rc, "tries": tries,
           "next": time.time() + 60 * 2 ** (tries - 1), "t": time.time()}
    os.makedirs(FAIL, exist_ok=True)
    wjson(os.path.join(FAIL, name + ".json"), rec)
    return rec


def give_up(name, f):
    """After MAX_TRIES failed tries: skip those messages, visibly; the rounds they opened stop waiting for name,
    and agents waiting for name's answer are woken (it isn't coming)."""
    seen(name, max(seen(name), max(f["ids"])))
    failure(name, clear=True)
    for q in open_rounds():
        if q in f["ids"]:
            hold_outcome(q, name, failed=True)
    for x in AGENTS:
        if x != name and name in ((asleep(x) or {}).get("from") or []):
            sleep_set(x, False)
    log_turn(name, f["ids"], "gave up", note=f"after {f['tries']} failed tries")


def sync():
    """Refresh the code snapshot from SRC (serialized: concurrent one-shot runs would race on the directory swap)."""
    if SRC and not os.path.isdir(SRC):
        sys.exit(f"agora: the source folder {SRC} is gone; run agora from the project folder, or --src DIR")
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(STATE, "sync.lock"), "w") as lk:
        lock(lk)
        return _sync()


def excluded(rel, pats):
    """rel (a /-separated path) is left out by pats. A glob (*, ?, [) matches the whole path or any one component;
    a SECRETS name matches any component; other patterns are path prefixes (data/, runs/). A trailing / means a
    directory."""
    from fnmatch import fnmatch
    parts = rel.split("/")
    for p in pats:
        name, d = p.rstrip("/"), p.endswith("/")
        comps = parts[:-1] if d else parts
        if any(c in p for c in "*?["):
            if fnmatch(rel, name) or any(fnmatch(c, name) for c in comps):
                return True
        elif p in SECRETS and name in comps or rel.startswith(p):
            return True
    return False


class TooBig(Exception):
    pass


def list_files(src):
    """src's files as /-separated relative paths: git-tracked plus untracked-not-ignored, for a plain folder (no
    git) every file .gitignore files don't exclude."""
    if git_top(src):
        cmd = ["git", "-C", src, "ls-files", "-z", "-co", "--exclude-standard"]
    else:   # a throwaway git dir lets git walk the folder and apply any .gitignore files in it
        g = os.path.join(STATE, "plain.git")
        if not os.path.isdir(g):
            subprocess.run(["git", "init", "-q", "--bare", g], capture_output=True, check=True)
        cmd = ["git", "--git-dir", g, "--work-tree", src, "-c", "core.bare=false", "ls-files", "-z", "-o",
               "--exclude-standard"]
    return [f for f in subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, check=True, cwd=src).stdout.decode(
        errors="surrogateescape").split("\0") if f]


def _snap(src, dest, exclude=()):
    """Copy src's files (see list_files) minus exclude and SECRETS into dest, swapped in whole; src None makes
    an empty snapshot. Over the size limits it raises TooBig and the old snapshot stays.
    Returns (file count, content digest, HEAD line)."""
    pats = tuple(exclude) + SECRETS
    files = list_files(src) if src else []
    root = os.path.realpath(src) + os.sep if src else ""
    big = float(CFG.get("max_file_mb", 20)) * 2**20
    skipped = []

    def ok(f):   # a regular file, not excluded, and (symlinks resolved) still inside the source, not excluded
        p = os.path.join(src, f)
        real = os.path.realpath(p)
        if excluded(f, pats) or not os.path.isfile(p) or not real.startswith(root) \
                or excluded(real[len(root):].replace(os.sep, "/"), pats) \
                or real.startswith(DATA + os.sep) or real.startswith(WS + os.sep):
            return False
        if os.path.getsize(p) > big:
            skipped.append(f)
            return False
        return True
    files = [f for f in files if ok(f)]
    max_files, max_mb = int(CFG.get("max_files", 20000)), float(CFG.get("max_mb", 500))
    if len(files) > max_files:
        raise TooBig(f"{len(files)} files (limit {max_files}, config max_files)")
    dig, total = __import__("hashlib").sha1(), 0
    for f in files:
        st = os.stat(os.path.join(src, f))
        total += st.st_size
        dig.update(f"{f}\0{st.st_size}\0{st.st_mtime_ns}\n".encode(errors="surrogateescape"))
    if total > max_mb * 2**20:
        raise TooBig(f"{total / 2**20:.0f} MB (limit {max_mb:.0f} MB, config max_mb)")
    new, old = dest + ".new", dest + ".old"
    shutil.rmtree(new, ignore_errors=True)
    for f in files:
        d = os.path.join(new, f)
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(d), exist_ok=True)
        shutil.copy2(os.path.join(src, f), d)
    os.makedirs(new, exist_ok=True)
    git = bool(src and git_top(src))
    head = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", src, "log", "-1", "--format=%h %s"], capture_output=True,
                          text=True).stdout if git else "(not a git repo)\n"
    hist = git and HISTORY and subprocess.run(["git", "clone", "--bare", "--quiet", src, os.path.join(new, ".git")],
                                              capture_output=True).returncode == 0
    if hist:   # the history, read-only: git log / show / diff / blame work in the snapshot
        subprocess.run(["git", "-C", new, "config", "core.bare", "false"], capture_output=True)
        subprocess.run(["git", "-C", new, "reset", "-q"], capture_output=True)   # index from HEAD; files untouched
    with open(os.path.join(new, "SNAPSHOT.txt"), "w") as fh:
        fh.write(f"Snapshot of {src} at {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')}, HEAD {head}"
                 f"{len(files)} files; excluded: {', '.join(exclude) or 'nothing'} plus "
                 + ("gitignored files" if git else "files .gitignore files exclude")
                 + ", secrets-like files (.env*, *.pem, *.key, ...)"
                 + (f" and {len(skipped)} files over {big / 2**20:.0f} MB" if skipped else "") + ".\n"
                 + ("Git history is in .git (git log/show/diff/blame); `git status` shows the excluded files as "
                    "deleted.\n" if hist else "") if src else
                 f"No source folder: this discussion has no code ({time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')}).\n")
    shutil.rmtree(old, ignore_errors=True)
    if os.path.exists(dest):
        os.rename(dest, old)
    os.rename(new, dest)
    shutil.rmtree(old, ignore_errors=True)
    return len(files), dig.hexdigest(), head


def _sync():
    try:
        n, dig, head = _snap(SRC, CODE, EXCLUDE)
    except TooBig as e:
        n = None
        print(f"agora: not refreshing the snapshot of {SRC}: {e}. Exclude big folders (`agora setup`, or "
              f"\"exclude\" in {CONFIG}); the previous snapshot stays.", file=sys.stderr)
        if not os.path.isdir(CODE):
            sys.exit(1)
        return None
    for name, path in ALSO.items():
        if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(path, ".git")) or os.path.realpath(path) == SRC:
            print(f"agora: skipping also.{name}: {path} is not a separate git repo", file=sys.stderr)
            continue
        try:
            dig += _snap(path, os.path.join(ALSO_DIR, name))[1]
        except TooBig as e:
            print(f"agora: not refreshing also.{name}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
    if os.path.isdir(ALSO_DIR):  # drop snapshots of repos no longer configured
        for d in os.listdir(ALSO_DIR):
            if d not in ALSO:
                shutil.rmtree(os.path.join(ALSO_DIR, d), ignore_errors=True)
    with open(os.path.join(STATE, "snapshot.json"), "w") as fh:  # content digest: sessions note real changes only
        json.dump({"digest": __import__("hashlib").sha1(dig.encode()).hexdigest()[:12], "head": head.strip()}, fh)
    return n


AUTO = tuple(CFG.get("serve") or AGENTS)  # agents the serve loop runs headlessly
SESS = os.path.join(STATE, "sessions")  # <name>.json: the agent's persistent CLI session


def session(name, val=None, drop=False):
    """Read (default), write (val) or drop an agent's session record."""
    f = os.path.join(SESS, name + ".json")
    if drop:
        if os.path.exists(f):
            os.unlink(f)
        return None
    if val is not None:
        os.makedirs(SESS, exist_ok=True)
        with open(f + ".tmp", "w") as g:
            json.dump(val, g)
        os.replace(f + ".tmp", f)
        return val
    try:
        return json.load(open(f))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def stale(name, s, phash):
    """Why session s must be replaced by a fresh one (None: resume it)."""
    if not s or not s.get("id"):
        return "no session"
    if s.get("turns", 0) >= MAX_TURNS:
        return f"{s['turns']} turns"
    if s.get("tokens", 0) >= MAX_TOKENS:
        return f"{s['tokens']} tokens"
    if s.get("proto") != phash:
        return "protocol changed"
    if s.get("src", SRC_ID) != SRC_ID:
        return "source folder changed"
    return None


def codex_event(name, e, res):
    if e.get("type") == "thread.started":
        res["sid"] = e.get("thread_id")
    it = e.get("item") or {}
    typ, key = it.get("type"), it.get("id")
    if e.get("type") == "item.started":
        if typ == "command_execution":
            act(name, key, describe_cmd(it.get("command", "")))
        elif typ == "web_search":
            act(name, key, "searching the web")
        elif typ == "mcp_tool_call":
            act(name, key, "calling " + str(it.get("tool", "a tool")))
        elif typ == "reasoning":
            busy(name, True, "thinking")
    elif e.get("type") == "item.completed":
        act(name, key)
        if typ == "agent_message":
            busy(name, True, "writing")
        elif typ in ("command_execution", "web_search", "mcp_tool_call"):
            busy(name, True, "thinking")


def codex_context(sid):
    """Current context size of codex session sid: input tokens of its latest model call, from the rollout log
    (the --json turn usage sums all calls of the turn, so it overstates the context)."""
    import glob
    for f in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(INSTALL, ".codex-home", "sessions", "*", "*", "*", f"*{sid}.jsonl")))[-1:]:
        last = 0
        for line in open(f):
            if '"token_count"' in line:
                try:
                    info = json.loads(line)["payload"].get("info") or {}
                    last = (info.get("last_token_usage") or {}).get("input_tokens", last)
                except (ValueError, KeyError, AttributeError):
                    pass
        return last
    return 0


def agy_event(name, e, res):
    if e.get("conversation_id"):
        res["sid"] = e["conversation_id"]
    if e.get("event") == "result":
        r = e.get("result") or {}
        res["text"], res["sid"] = r.get("response", ""), r.get("conversation_id") or res.get("sid")
        return
    su = e.get("step_update") or {}
    u = su.get("usage")
    if u:  # context of the latest model call (the result's usage is cumulative over the conversation)
        res["tokens"] = (u.get("input_tokens") or 0) + (u.get("cache_read_tokens") or 0)
    key, st = su.get("step_index"), su.get("state")
    if su.get("step_type") == "tool":
        if st == "ACTIVE":
            info = su.get("tool_info") or {}
            pr = info.get("parameters") or {}
            bg = bool(pr.get("WaitMsBeforeAsync")) or bool(pr.get("Background") or pr.get("RunInBackground"))
            act(name, key, describe_tool(su.get("tool_name", "tool"), pr), bg=bg)
        else:
            act(name, key)
            busy(name, True, "thinking")
    elif su.get("step_type") == "agent_response" and st == "ACTIVE":
        busy(name, True, "writing")


def stream(name, cmd, stdin_text, cwd, env, log, timeout, on_event):
    """Run an agent CLI that prints JSONL events, feeding each to on_event (activity tracking); returns the process."""
    import threading
    p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, cwd=cwd, env=env, text=True, stdin=subprocess.PIPE if stdin_text else subprocess.DEVNULL,
                         stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=log)
    killer = threading.Timer(timeout, p.kill)   # started first: a child that never reads its stdin is killed too
    killer.start()
    try:
        if stdin_text:
            try:
                p.stdin.write(stdin_text)
                p.stdin.close()
            except (BrokenPipeError, OSError) as ex:
                log.write(f"[stdin] {ex!r}\n")
        for line in p.stdout:
            try:
                e = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                log.write(line)
                continue
            try:
                on_event(name, e)
            except Exception as ex:  # activity display must never break a turn
                log.write(f"[activity] {ex!r}\n")
        p.wait()
    finally:
        killer.cancel()
    return p


def rules(name):
    return ("Output ONLY your message text "
            "(no preamble). Optionally make the first line `TO: name1,name2` (default: the author of the "
            "latest message), and a line `RE: 12,14` naming the messages you answer (default: all the new ones "
            "addressed to you). If you have nothing worth adding, output only `SLEEP`: nothing is posted and you "
            "stop answering messages to all until someone pings you (`@" + name + "` or addresses you by name). "
            "A first line `SLEEP` before a message posts it and then sleeps. To hold off until a specific "
            "participant has replied (e.g. you asked codex to check something), use a first line `WAIT: codex` "
            "(with or without a message after it): you skip everything until codex posts, then get a turn. "
            "Sleeping is automatic too: after a message addressed only to other agents you wait for their answer; "
            "a ping or the user writing to all wakes you. Questions to all are answered by one agent first; if "
            "another agent has already answered what you were asked, reply only with a correction or something "
            "new, otherwise output only `SLEEP`.\n\n"
            "EVIDENCE (rules 1-2): cite path:line for claims about the code and say what you didn't check; check "
            "another agent's claim in the code before agreeing with it.\n")


LENGTH = {
    "short": "LENGTH (rule 3): 1-5 short lines, about 600 characters: the answer, its evidence, and at most one "
             "line of qualification that changes the conclusion. Go longer only if the user asked for an audit, "
             "review, report or design, and then lead with a one-line summary. No recap of the thread.",
    "long": "LENGTH (rule 3, {mode} request): start with a one-line summary, then short bullets, one finding each, "
            "with path:line evidence, then what you didn't check. As long as the content needs, no longer: no "
            "preamble, recap or closing summary.",
    "independent": "INDEPENDENT ROUND: the others answer the same question without seeing your answer, and all "
                   "answers are revealed together afterwards. Give your own full answer; do not output SLEEP because "
                   "someone else may cover it. ",
    "crosscheck": "CROSS-CHECK: the independent answers to #{q} were just revealed together. Say where the others "
                  "are wrong or missed something, citing code, and whether any of them changed your mind; output "
                  "only SLEEP if you agree and have nothing to add.",
}


def turn_note(new_msgs):
    """The length and round instructions for a turn answering new_msgs."""
    modes = {m.get("mode") for m in new_msgs if m["from"] == "user"}
    rev = sorted({m["independent"] for m in new_msgs if m.get("independent")})
    s = ""
    if "independent" in modes:
        s += LENGTH["independent"]
    long = next((x for x in ("audit", "design", "independent") if x in modes), None)
    s += LENGTH["long"].format(mode=long) if long else LENGTH["short"]
    if rev:
        s += " " + LENGTH["crosscheck"].format(q=", #".join(map(str, rev)))
    return s + "\n"


def snapshot_head():
    """(content digest, HEAD line) of the current code snapshot."""
    try:
        d = json.load(open(os.path.join(STATE, "snapshot.json")))
        return d["digest"], d["head"]
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError):
        return "", ""


def opt(name, key, default=None):
    """Per-agent setting: env AGORA_<NAME>_<KEY>, else "<name>_<key>" in agora.json, else default."""
    return os.environ.get(f"AGORA_{name.upper()}_{key.upper()}") or CFG.get(f"{name}_{key}") or default


def agent_cmd(name, sid, work, out):
    """The CLI command for one turn of name: fresh when sid is None, else resuming session sid.
    Returns (cmd, prompt_on_stdin)."""
    if name == "codex":  # codex exec resume has no -C: the cwd (work) is the workspace either way
        base = ["codex", "exec"] + (["resume"] if sid else []) + ["--json", "--skip-git-repo-check"]
        return base + ([] if sid else ["-C", work]) + [
            "-c", "model_reasoning_effort=" + opt("codex", "effort", "medium")] + (
            ["-c", "model=" + json.dumps(opt("codex", "model"))] if opt("codex", "model") else []) + [
            "-o", out] + codex_perms() + ([sid] if sid else []) + ["-"], True
    if name == "gemini":  # Antigravity print mode: workspace = code snapshot + work dir; approvals auto-denied
        return [AGY, "--model", opt("gemini", "model", "gemini-4-hydrogen-high"),
                "--add-dir", CODE] + (["--add-dir", ALSO_DIR] if ALSO else []) + [
                "--input-format", "stream-json", "--output-format", "stream-json"] + (
                ["--conversation", sid] if sid else []) + ["-p="], True   # prompt on stdin, not in argv
    # claude: Claude Code print mode on the local login, read-only tools plus a sandboxed shell; no user
    # settings/hooks, MCP servers or skills (they cost ~150k context tokens per turn); prompt on stdin
    shell = claude_sandbox(work)
    cmd = [CLAUDE, "-p", "--output-format", "stream-json", "--verbose", "--setting-sources", "project,local",
           "--strict-mcp-config", "--disable-slash-commands", "--add-dir", CODE] + (["--add-dir", ALSO_DIR] if ALSO else []) + [
           "--tools", "Read", "Grep", "Glob"] + (["Bash", "--settings", json.dumps(shell)] if shell else [])
    for key in ("model", "effort"):
        if opt("claude", key):
            cmd += ["--" + key, opt("claude", key)]
    return cmd + (["--resume", sid] if sid else []), True


def codex_perms():
    """-c overrides granting this workspace's paths to the permission profile set in agora's Codex home, if any
    (its config names the install's own paths only). Entries add to the profile's; its denies stay."""
    if WS == INSTALL:
        return []
    try:
        cfg = open(os.path.join(INSTALL, ".codex-home", "config.toml")).read()
    except OSError:
        return []
    m = re.search(r'(?m)^default_permissions\s*=\s*"([\w-]+)"', cfg)
    if not m or f"[permissions.{m.group(1)}" not in cfg:
        return []
    fs = {CODE: "read", MD: "read", STATE: "deny"}
    if ALSO:
        fs[ALSO_DIR] = "read"
    if SRC:
        fs[SRC] = "deny"   # the live tree: agents read the snapshot
    return ["-c", f"permissions.{m.group(1)}.filesystem={{" + ", ".join(f"{json.dumps(k)}={json.dumps(v)}"
                                                                       for k, v in fs.items()) + "}"]


def claude_sandbox(work):
    """Claude Code settings giving headless claude a shell like codex's: commands run in Claude Code's OS sandbox
    (bubblewrap on Linux, Seatbelt on macOS), reading only the snapshots and its work dir, writing only its work
    dir, with no network. None (no shell) when off in the config or the sandbox can't run here."""
    on = os.environ.get("AGORA_CLAUDE_SHELL", CFG.get("claude_shell", True))
    if str(on).lower() in ("false", "0", "no", "off") or sys.platform not in ("linux", "darwin"):
        return None
    if sys.platform == "linux" and not (shutil.which("bwrap") and shutil.which("socat")):
        return None
    deny = sorted({os.path.expanduser("~"), "/root", "/home", "/Users", "/mnt", "/media", "/srv", "/Volumes", INSTALL,
                   WS, DATA} | ({SRC} if SRC else set()) | {os.path.realpath(p) for p in ALSO.values()})
    return {"sandbox": {"enabled": True, "autoAllowBashIfSandboxed": True, "allowUnsandboxedCommands": False,
                        "network": {"allowedDomains": []},
                        "filesystem": {"denyRead": deny, "allowRead": [CODE, ALSO_DIR, work],
                                       "denyWrite": [CODE, ALSO_DIR]}}}


def can_shell(name):
    return name != "claude" or claude_sandbox(os.path.join(WS, "work", "claude")) is not None


def agent_env(name):
    """Local CLI logins only: drop API keys (they would switch the CLIs to API billing) and, for claude, the
    variables that tie a nested Claude Code to the session that started agora."""
    drop = {"OPENAI_API_KEY", "CODEX_API_KEY", "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"}
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items()
           if k not in drop and not (name == "claude" and (k.startswith("CLAUDE_CODE_") or k in ("CLAUDECODE", "CLAUDE_PID", "CLAUDE_EFFORT")))}
    if name == "codex":
        env["CODEX_HOME"] = os.path.join(INSTALL, ".codex-home")
    return env


def invoke(name, sid, prompt, work, log, timeout):
    """One CLI run of name (fresh when sid is None, else resuming sid). Returns (process, text, res)."""
    out = os.path.join(STATE, name + "_last.md")
    if os.path.exists(out):
        os.unlink(out)
    res = {}
    cmd, on_stdin = agent_cmd(name, sid, work, out)
    if not on_stdin:
        cmd.append("-p=" + prompt)
    elif name == "gemini":   # agy reads stream-json events on stdin
        prompt = json.dumps({"event": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": prompt}}) + "\n"
    handler = {"codex": codex_event, "gemini": agy_event, "claude": claude_event}[name]
    r = stream(name, cmd, prompt if on_stdin else None, work, agent_env(name), log, timeout,
               lambda n, e: handler(n, e, res))
    text = (open(out).read() if name == "codex" and os.path.exists(out) else res.get("text") or "").strip()
    if name != "codex":
        log.write(text + "\n")
    if name == "codex" and res.get("sid"):
        res["tokens"] = codex_context(res["sid"])
    return r, text, res


HANDOFF = ("Your session is about to be replaced by a fresh one ({why}); it will get the protocol and the whole "
           "thread again, but not your private working memory. Write a handoff note for it, at most 1500 characters: "
           "open questions, live hypotheses, checks you meant to do, and key facts with path:line. Output only the "
           "note; it is not posted to the thread.")


def run_agent(name, timeout=1800, do_sync=True, served=False):
    """One turn of name at a time (serve and a one-shot `agora NAME` would otherwise answer the same messages)."""
    with lockfile(name + ".run.lock") as lk:
        lock(lk)
        if served and not any(m["id"] > seen(name) and for_me(m, name) for m in load()):
            return "nothing"   # answered by a one-shot run while this one waited
        return _run_agent(name, timeout, do_sync)


def _run_agent(name, timeout=1800, do_sync=True):
    """Run one headless turn of an agent on the thread and post its reply. Resumes the agent's persistent
    session with just the unseen messages, or starts a fresh one (see stale())."""
    if do_sync:
        sync()
    msgs = load()
    thread = "".join(fmt(m) for m in msgs)
    if len(thread) > 200_000:
        thread = "[earlier messages truncated; full thread in " + MD + "]\n\n" + thread[-200_000:]
    new_msgs = [m for m in msgs if for_me(m, name) and m["id"] > seen(name)]
    new = [m["id"] for m in new_msgs]
    note = turn_note(new_msgs)
    asked = [q for q in open_rounds() if q in new]   # independent rounds this turn answers
    work = os.path.join(WS, "work", name)
    os.makedirs(work, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(work, "THREAD.md"), "w") as f:   # decisions first: they survive the truncation
        f.write("# Thread so far\n\n" + decisions_text(msgs) + thread)
    proto = protocol()
    phash = __import__("hashlib").sha1((proto + rules(name)).encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    head, head_line = snapshot_head()
    fresh_prompt = (proto + f"\n\n# You are: {name}\n\nThe codebase is at {CODE} (read-only). " + also_note() + "The full thread is in "
                    f"{work}/THREAD.md: read it first. Reply to the new message(s) addressed to you: {new}. "
                    "Only read files under the codebase" + (", the extra snapshots" if ALSO else "") + " and that thread file. "
                    + ("You can run read-only shell commands there (git log/show/blame, grep, tests that don't need "
                       "the network). " if can_shell(name) else "") + rules(name)
                    + note)
    log = open(os.path.join(STATE, name + ".log"), "a")
    s = session(name)
    why = stale(name, s, phash)
    if why and why.endswith(("turns", "tokens")):  # a cap, not a fault: let the old session hand over first
        log.write(f"\n=== {time.ctime()} handoff from {s['id']} ({why})\n")
        log.flush()
        busy(name, True, "writing a handoff note")
        r, note, _ = invoke(name, s["id"], HANDOFF.format(why=why), work, log, min(timeout, 600))
        if r.returncode == 0 and note:
            fresh_prompt += ("\n\n# Handoff note from your previous session (private, not in the thread)\n\n"
                             + note[:3000] + "\n")
    for attempt in (0, 1):
        if why:
            s, prompt = None, fresh_prompt
        else:
            unseen = [m for m in msgs if m["id"] > s.get("upto", 0) and m["from"] != name]
            prompt = ("# New in the thread since your last turn\n\n" + ("".join(fmt(m) for m in unseen) or "(nothing)\n")
                      + (f"\nThe code snapshot at {CODE} changed since your last turn (HEAD {head_line}); re-read files you rely on. " + also_note() + "\n"
                         if head != s.get("head") else "")
                      + f"\nReply to the message(s) addressed to you: {new}. Same rules as before: " + rules(name) + note)
        log.write(f"\n=== {time.ctime()} replying to {new}: " + (f"fresh session ({why})" if why else
                  f"resuming {s['id']} (turn {s.get('turns', 0) + 1})") + "\n")
        log.flush()
        r, text, res = invoke(name, s and s["id"], prompt, work, log, timeout)
        if r.returncode == 0 and text and res.get("sid"):
            session(name, {"id": res["sid"], "turns": (s or {}).get("turns", 0) + 1, "tokens": res.get("tokens", 0),
                           "upto": msgs[-1]["id"] if msgs else 0, "proto": phash, "head": head, "src": SRC_ID,
                           "started": (s or {}).get("started") or time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")})
            break
        session(name, drop=True)  # never resume a session whose last turn failed
        if why or r.returncode < 0:  # a fresh run failed, or the turn was killed (timeout): don't retry
            break
        why = f"resume failed (rc {r.returncode})"
        log.write(why + "; retrying fresh\n")
    if r.returncode or not text:   # the messages stay unseen: serve retries with backoff, then gives up visibly
        f = note_failure(name, new, r.returncode)
        log_turn(name, new, "failed", note=f"rc {r.returncode}, try {f['tries']}/{MAX_TRIES}")
        print(f"{name} failed (rc {r.returncode}); see {STATE}/{name}.log", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    to, zz, wf, re_ = msgs[-1]["from"] if msgs else "all", False, [], list(new)
    for _ in range(4):  # directive lines: TO: ..., RE: ..., SLEEP, WAIT: name, in any order
        first, _, rest = text.strip().partition("\n")
        d = first.strip().strip("`*")
        if d.upper().startswith("TO:"):
            to, text = d[3:].strip(), rest
        elif d.rstrip(".").upper() == "SLEEP":
            zz, text = True, rest
        elif d.upper().startswith("RE:"):
            ids = [int(x) for x in re.findall(r"\d+", d[3:]) if 0 < int(x) <= len(msgs)]
            re_, text = ids or re_, rest
        elif d.upper().startswith("WAIT:"):
            wf = [x.strip().lower() for x in d[5:].split(",") if x.strip().lower() in NAMES and x.strip().lower() != name]
            zz, text = True, rest
    sleep_set(name, False)
    m = post(name, to, text, hold=asked, re_=re_) if text.strip() else None
    if msgs:   # read only once the reply is out: a crash before this retries the turn instead of losing it
        seen(name, max(seen(name), msgs[-1]["id"]))
    failure(name, clear=True)
    if m and m.get("held"):
        log_turn(name, new, "held", note="independent round " + ", ".join(f"#{q}" for q in m["rounds"]))
        return m
    for q in asked:   # slept without answering an independent round it was asked: don't wait for it
        hold_outcome(q, name, slept=True)
    log_turn(name, new, "posted" if m else "slept", msg=m and m["id"])
    if zz:
        sleep_set(name, True, why="waiting for " + ",".join(wf) if wf else "nothing to add", until_from=wf)
        # no deadlock: whoever waits on name gets the turn if name waits on them (e.g. name was the lead) or if
        # name went quiet without posting (their wait would otherwise only end on the timeout)
        for x in AGENTS:
            if x != name and name in ((asleep(x) or {}).get("from") or []) and (x in wf or not m):
                sleep_set(x, False)
                print(f"{x} was waiting for {name}; woken", file=sys.stderr)
        print(f"{name} " + (f"waits for {','.join(wf)}" if wf else "sleeps until pinged"), file=sys.stderr)
    return m or ("slept" if zz else None)


def agent_streak(msgs):
    n = 0
    for m in reversed(msgs):
        if m["from"] == "user":
            break
        n += 1
    return n


COLORS = {"user": "1;37", "claude": "38;5;209", "codex": "38;5;114", "gemini": "38;5;75"}
ACT = os.path.join(STATE, "activity")  # <name>.json per agent working on a reply: phase + running actions


def _act_rw(name, fn, existing=False):
    os.makedirs(ACT, exist_ok=True)
    p = os.path.join(ACT, name + ".json")
    with open(p + ".lock", "a") as lk:
        fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        if existing and not os.path.exists(p):
            return
        try:
            a = json.load(open(p))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            a = {"phase": "thinking", "items": {}}
        a = fn(a)
        if a is None:
            if os.path.exists(p):
                os.unlink(p)
        else:
            a["t"] = time.time()
            with open(p + ".tmp", "w") as f:
                json.dump(a, f)
            os.replace(p + ".tmp", p)


def busy(name, on=True, phase="thinking"):
    """Mark an agent as working (phase text) or done (removes everything it was doing)."""
    _act_rw(name, (lambda a: {**a, "phase": phase}) if on else (lambda a: None))


FG_STALE = 1200   # a foreground action with no "done" after 20 min was interrupted (its post hook never ran)


def live_items(items, now):
    """An agent's actions minus finished ones whose short display time ran out and interrupted foreground ones."""
    return {k: v for k, v in items.items() if v.get("until", now + 1) > now
            and (v.get("bg") or now - v.get("since", now) < FG_STALE)}


def act(name, key, what=None, bg=False, existing=False):
    """Start (what given) or finish (what None) one concurrent action of an agent, e.g. a command."""
    def f(a):
        now = time.time()
        a["items"] = live_items(a["items"], now)
        if what is None:
            it = a["items"].get(str(key))
            if it and now - it["since"] < 1.5:  # keep quick actions on screen long enough to read
                it["until"] = it["since"] + 1.5
            else:
                a["items"].pop(str(key), None)
        else:
            a["items"][str(key)] = {"what": what, "bg": bg, "since": time.time()}
        return a
    _act_rw(name, f, existing)


def claude_hook(phase):
    """Claude Code Pre/PostToolUse hook: show claude's tool calls while it is working on a reply.
    No-op unless the hook's session is the one in state/claude.session and claude is already busy."""
    try:
        d = json.load(sys.stdin)
        want = open(os.path.join(STATE, "claude.session")).read().strip()
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return
    if not want or d.get("session_id") != want:
        return
    tool, inp = d.get("tool_name", ""), d.get("tool_input") or {}
    key = d.get("tool_use_id") or tool
    if phase == "post":
        return act("claude", key, None, existing=True)
    what = claude_tool_text(tool, inp)
    if what:
        act("claude", key, what, bg=bool(inp.get("run_in_background")), existing=True)


def claude_tool_text(tool, inp):
    """Claude Code tool call -> short activity text (None: don't show)."""
    if tool == "Bash":
        cmd = inp.get("command", "")
        return None if "/agora " in cmd or cmd.startswith("agora ") else describe_cmd(cmd)
    if tool in ("Read", "Edit", "Write"):
        f = (inp.get("file_path") or "").replace(CODE + "/", "")
        return ("reading " if tool == "Read" else "editing ") + os.path.basename(f) if "/agora/" not in f else "reading " + f
    if tool in ("Grep", "Glob"):
        return f"searching `{(inp.get('pattern') or '')[:30]}`"
    if tool.startswith("Web") or "exa" in tool:
        return "searching the web"
    if tool == "Agent":
        return "running a subagent"
    return None


def claude_event(name, e, res):
    """Headless Claude Code (stream-json) event: activity, session id, reply text, context size."""
    t = e.get("type")
    if e.get("session_id"):
        res["sid"] = e["session_id"]
    if t == "assistant":
        msg = e.get("message") or {}
        u = msg.get("usage") or {}
        if u:  # context of the latest model call
            res["tokens"] = sum(u.get(k) or 0 for k in ("input_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens", "cache_creation_input_tokens"))
        for c in msg.get("content") or []:
            if c.get("type") == "tool_use":
                act(name, c.get("id"), claude_tool_text(c.get("name", ""), c.get("input") or {}) or c.get("name", "tool"))
            elif c.get("type") in ("thinking", "redacted_thinking"):
                busy(name, True, "thinking")
            elif c.get("type") == "text":
                busy(name, True, "writing")
    elif t == "user":
        for c in (e.get("message") or {}).get("content") or []:
            if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("type") == "tool_result":
                act(name, c.get("tool_use_id"))
                busy(name, True, "thinking")
    elif t == "result":
        res["text"] = "" if e.get("is_error") else (e.get("result") or "")


def busy_now():
    """{name: activity} for agents working on a reply (stale after ~30 min without any update)."""
    out = {}
    try:
        for fn in os.listdir(ACT):
            if fn.endswith(".json"):
                try:
                    a = json.load(open(os.path.join(ACT, fn)))
                except (OSError, ValueError):
                    continue
                if time.time() - a.get("t", 0) < 1900:
                    a["items"] = live_items(a.get("items", {}), time.time())
                    out[fn[:-5]] = a
    except OSError:
        pass
    return dict(sorted(out.items()))


def describe_cmd(cmd):
    """Turn a shell command into 'reading x' / 'searching y' / 'running `z`'."""
    import re, shlex
    m = re.match(r"^(?:/bin/)?(?:ba)?sh -l?c (.*)$", cmd.strip(), re.S)
    if m:
        try:
            cmd = shlex.split(m.group(1))[0]
        except ValueError:
            cmd = m.group(1).strip("'\"")
    cmd = cmd.replace(CODE + "/", "").replace(CODE, "code").strip()
    if "\n" in cmd:   # multi-line (heredoc / script): first line only, so the status line never wraps
        cmd = cmd.split("\n", 1)[0].rstrip() + " …"
    try:
        w = shlex.split(cmd)
    except ValueError:
        w = cmd.split()
    if not w:
        return "running a command"
    files = [x for x in w[1:] if not x.startswith("-") and ("/" in x or "." in x) and " " not in x]
    if w[0] in ("cat", "sed", "head", "tail", "nl", "less", "bat") and "|" not in cmd and files:
        return "reading " + ", ".join(files[-2:])
    if w[0] in ("rg", "grep", "ag", "git") and "|" not in cmd:
        pat = next((x for x in w[1:] if not x.startswith("-")), "")
        return f"searching `{pat[:30]}`" if pat else "searching"
    if w[0] in ("ls", "find", "tree", "fd"):
        return "listing " + (files[0] if files else "files")
    return f"running `{cmd[:50]}{'…' if len(cmd) > 50 else ''}`"


def describe_tool(tool, params):
    """Antigravity tool step -> short activity text."""
    params = params or {}
    if "CommandLine" in params:
        return describe_cmd(params["CommandLine"])
    path = next((v for k, v in params.items() if isinstance(v, str) and ("Path" in k or "File" in k or k.lower() == "path")), None)
    if path:
        path = path.replace(CODE + "/", "")
        if "view" in tool or "read" in tool:
            return "reading " + path
        if "list" in tool or "dir" in tool:
            return "listing " + path
    q = next((v for k, v in params.items() if isinstance(v, str) and ("Query" in k or "Pattern" in k)), None)
    if q:
        return f"searching `{q[:30]}`"
    return tool.replace("_", " ")


def sleep_summary(zz):
    """One line naming every sleeping agent and what wakes it."""
    if not zz:
        return "everyone awake"
    parts = []
    for n in sorted(zz):
        wf = (asleep(n) or {}).get("from")
        parts.append(n + (f" (waiting for {', '.join(wf)})" if wf else ""))
    return "💤 asleep: " + ", ".join(parts) + " — @name pings one awake"


def act_text(a):
    """One agent's activity as plain text."""
    now = time.time()
    items = sorted((x for x in a.get("items", {}).values() if x.get("until", now + 1) > now), key=lambda x: x["since"])
    if not items:
        return a.get("phase", "thinking")
    fg = [x for x in items if not x["bg"]]
    bg = [x for x in items if x["bg"]]
    parts = []
    if fg:
        parts.append(fg[0]["what"] + (f" +{len(fg) - 1} more" if len(fg) > 1 else ""))
    if bg:
        parts.append(f"{len(bg)} in background" if fg or len(bg) > 1 else bg[0]["what"] + " (background)")
    return " ".join(", ".join(parts).split())   # one line, whatever the tool text held


def lock(f, shared=False, block=True):
    """Lock the open file f (exclusive, or shared). With block=False: False when someone else holds it."""
    try:
        fcntl.flock(f, (fcntl.LOCK_SH if shared else fcntl.LOCK_EX) | (0 if block else fcntl.LOCK_NB))
        return True
    except BlockingIOError:
        return False


def lockfile(name):
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    return open(os.path.join(STATE, name), "a+")


def serve_lock():
    """Take the serve lock (state/serve.lock) without blocking: the open file while held, None if another serve
    holds it. The lock dies with its process, so a crashed serve never blocks the next one."""
    f = lockfile("serve.lock")
    if not lock(f, block=False):
        f.close()
        return None
    f.seek(0); f.truncate(); f.write(str(os.getpid())); f.flush()
    return f


CLIENT = None


def client():
    """Mark this process as a client (chat, post, wait, post --via) until it exits: an idle `serve` started by
    agora only shuts down while no client holds this shared lock. Blocks while a serve is deciding to exit, so
    the serve-lock check that follows is accurate."""
    global CLIENT
    if CLIENT is None:
        CLIENT = lockfile("clients.lock")
        lock(CLIENT, shared=True)
    return CLIENT


def serve_policy(only=None, budget=None, save=False):
    """The launch options (--only, --budget) an auto-started serve uses: the last ones given to `agora serve`."""
    p = os.path.join(STATE, "serve.json")
    if save:
        os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        with open(p, "w") as f:
            json.dump({"only": only, "budget": budget}, f)
    return _json(p)


def ensure_serve():
    """Start `agora serve` in the background (log: state/serve.log) unless one is running or autoserve is off."""
    client()
    if not CFG.get("autoserve", True) or os.environ.get("AGORA_AUTOSERVE", "1") == "0" or not AUTO:
        return
    with lockfile("spawn.lock") as sp:   # one starter at a time: two clients must not both start a serve
        lock(sp)
        f = serve_lock()
        if f is None:
            return   # already running
        f.close()    # free it for the child
        pol = serve_policy()
        log = open(os.path.join(STATE, "serve.log"), "a")
        subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, SCRIPT, "--dir", WS, "serve", "--auto"]
                         + (["--only", pol["only"]] if pol.get("only") else [])
                         + (["--budget", str(pol["budget"])] if pol.get("budget") else []),
                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, start_new_session=True, cwd=WS)
        for _ in range(100):   # until the child holds the serve lock (so the next starter sees it running)
            time.sleep(0.1)
            f = serve_lock()
            if f is None:
                break
            f.close()
    print(f"started agora serve for {', '.join(pol.get('only', '').split(',') if pol.get('only') else AUTO)} "
          f"(log: {os.path.join(STATE, 'serve.log')})", file=sys.stderr)


def vwidth(s):
    """Terminal columns a string takes: wide East Asian chars and most emoji 2, combining marks 0, and an emoji
    joined on by a zero-width joiner or a skin-tone modifier nothing (they draw as one glyph)."""
    import unicodedata
    w, joined = 0, False
    for c in s:
        if joined or unicodedata.combining(c) or c in "\u200d\ufe0e\ufe0f" or "\U0001f3fb" <= c <= "\U0001f3ff":
            joined = c == "\u200d"
            continue
        w += 2 if unicodedata.east_asian_width(c) in "WF" else 1
    return w


def clip(s, width):
    """s cut to at most width columns, with … when cut."""
    if vwidth(s) <= width:
        return s
    out, w = "", 0
    for c in s:
        w += vwidth(c)
        if w > width - 1:
            break
        out += c
    return out + "…"


def chat(to="all", after=None):
    """Live view: prints every new message as it lands and reads your replies from the prompt."""
    ensure_serve()
    import readline, threading  # noqa: F401  (readline gives line editing + history to input())
    tty = sys.stdout.isatty()
    col = (lambda c, t: f"\033[{c}m{t}\033[0m") if tty else (lambda c, t: t)
    state = {"to": to, "last": after if after is not None else (load()[-1]["id"] if load() else 0),
             "busy": {}, "stop": False, "mine": set(), "shown": False, "frame": 0, "reading": False,
             "toff": os.path.getsize(TURNS) if os.path.exists(TURNS) else 0}
    lock = threading.Lock()

    def plain_prompt():
        return f"[to {state['to']}] > "

    def prompt():   # for our own writes
        return col("2", f"[to {state['to']}] ") + "> "

    def rl_prompt():   # for input(): escapes inside \001…\002 so readline counts only the visible characters
        return f"\001\033[2m\002[to {state['to']}] \001\033[0m\002> " if tty else plain_prompt()

    try:   # readline's cursor position (a byte offset in the line), for redraws while you edit mid-line
        import ctypes
        rl_point = ctypes.c_int.in_dll(ctypes.CDLL(readline.__file__), "rl_point")
    except Exception:
        rl_point = None

    def up():
        """Rows from the cursor up to the prompt's first row."""
        if not state["reading"]:
            return 0
        buf = readline.get_line_buffer()
        if rl_point is not None:
            buf = buf.encode()[:max(0, rl_point.value)].decode(errors="ignore")
        return (vwidth(plain_prompt()) + vwidth(buf)) // max(1, shutil.get_terminal_size().columns)

    def mv(n):
        return f"\033[{n}A" if n > 0 else ""

    SPIN = "⠋⠙⠹⠸⠼⠴⠦⠧⠇⠏"

    def zz_text():
        zz = state.get("zz") or {}
        return ("💤 " + ", ".join(n + (f" (waits for {', '.join(w)})" if w else "") for n, w in sorted(zz.items()))
                if zz else "")

    def has_line():
        return tty and bool(state["busy"] or state.get("zz") or state.get("notes"))

    def notes_text():
        return "  ".join(state.get("notes") or [])

    def typing_line():
        """The status line above the prompt: who is working on what, then who is asleep."""
        width = shutil.get_terminal_size().columns - 1
        nt = notes_text()
        if not state["busy"]:
            z = "  ".join(x for x in (nt, zz_text()) if x)
            return col("33" if nt else "2", clip(z, width))
        out, used = col("2", SPIN[state["frame"] % len(SPIN)]), 1
        for n, a in state["busy"].items():
            room = width - used - len(n) - 5
            if room < 8:
                out += col("2", " …")
                break
            what = clip(act_text(a), room)
            out += (col("2", " ·") if used > 1 else "") + " " + col(COLORS.get(n, "0"), n) + " " + col("2", what)
            used += len(n) + vwidth(what) + 4
        for z, c in ((nt, "33"), (zz_text(), "2")):
            if z and width - used > 12:
                z = clip("  " + z, width - used)
                out += col(c, z)
                used += vwidth(z)
        return out

    def emit(text):
        """Print above the prompt, keeping the typing line (if any) directly above what you are typing."""
        with lock:
            buf = readline.get_line_buffer()
            out = "\r" + mv(up() + (1 if state["shown"] else 0)) + "\033[J" + text + "\n"
            state["shown"] = has_line()
            if state["shown"]:
                out += typing_line() + "\n"
            sys.stdout.write(out + (prompt() + hl_input(buf) if state["reading"] else ""))  # else input() draws it
            sys.stdout.flush()

    def hl_input(buf):
        """The typed line with pings coloured, including every name in a leading @a,b recipient list."""
        lead = re.match(r"@[\w,]+", buf) if tty else None
        if not lead:
            return pings(buf)
        names = lead.group(0)[1:].split(",")
        head = pings("@" + names[0]) + "".join("," + (f"\033[1;{COLORS[n.lower()].removeprefix('1;')}m{n}\033[22;39m"
                                                     if n.lower() in COLORS else n) for n in names[1:])
        return head + pings(buf[lead.end():])

    def paint_input():
        """Colour @name pings in the line being typed. readline draws it plain; this repaints the same characters in
        place (cursor saved and restored), so readline's view of the screen stays right; wrapped lines included."""
        buf = readline.get_line_buffer()
        if buf == state.get("painted") or not state["reading"]:
            return
        before, state["painted"] = state.get("painted") or "", buf
        if "@" not in buf and "@" not in before:
            return
        sys.stdout.write("\0337" + mv(up()) + "\r" + prompt() + hl_input(buf) + "\033[J\0338")
        sys.stdout.flush()

    def animate():
        while not state["stop"]:
            time.sleep(0.05)
            if not tty:
                continue
            with lock:
                paint_input()
                state["frame"] += 1
                if state["frame"] % 2:
                    continue
                line = typing_line() if has_line() else None
                if line is not None and state["shown"]:  # redraw the line above the prompt in place
                    if line == state.get("drawn"):
                        continue
                    sys.stdout.write("\0337" + mv(up() + 1) + "\r\033[K" + line + "\0338")
                elif line is not None:
                    sys.stdout.write("\r" + mv(up()) + "\033[J" + line + "\n" + (prompt() + hl_input(readline.get_line_buffer()) if state["reading"] else ""))
                    state["shown"] = True
                elif state["shown"]:
                    sys.stdout.write("\r" + mv(up() + 1) + "\033[J" + (prompt() + hl_input(readline.get_line_buffer()) if state["reading"] else ""))
                    state["shown"] = False
                else:
                    continue
                state["drawn"] = line
                sys.stdout.flush()

    def pings(out):  # @name mentions in bold, in that participant's colour
        if not tty:
            return out
        def hl(g):
            c = COLORS.get(g.group(1).lower(), "37").removeprefix("1;")
            return f"\033[1;{c}m{g.group(0)}\033[22;39m"
        return re.sub(r"(?<![\w@])@(" + "|".join(NAMES + ("all",)) + r")\b", hl, out, flags=re.I)

    def show(m):
        head = (col(COLORS.get(m["from"], "0"), f"── #{m['id']} {author(m)}") + col("2", f" → {', '.join(m['to'])}")
                + col("35", tag(m)) + col("2", f" · {m['ts'][11:]}"))
        emit(head + "\n" + pings(md(m["text"])))

    def md(text):
        if not tty:
            return text.rstrip() + "\n"
        try:
            import io
            from rich.console import Console
            from rich.markdown import Markdown
            buf = io.StringIO()
            Console(file=buf, force_terminal=True, width=min(shutil.get_terminal_size().columns, 110)).print(
                Markdown(text, code_theme="ansi_dark", hyperlinks=False))
            return buf.getvalue().rstrip() + "\n"
        except Exception:
            return text.rstrip() + "\n"

    def follow():
        while not state["stop"]:
            for m in load():
                if m["id"] > state["last"]:
                    state["last"] = m["id"]
                    if m["id"] not in state["mine"]:  # your own lines are already on screen
                        show(m)
            state["busy"] = busy_now()
            notes = []
            for q in open_rounds():
                notes.append(f"◆ #{q} independent: {len(round_status(q))}/{len(round_members())} in")
            if os.path.exists(os.path.join(STATE, "halted")):
                notes.append("⏸ budget reached: agents wait for you")
            state["notes"] = notes
            try:
                with open(TURNS) as fh:
                    fh.seek(state["toff"])
                    chunk = fh.read()
                chunk = chunk[:chunk.rfind("\n") + 1]   # whole lines only; a half-written one waits
                state["toff"] += len(chunk.encode())
            except OSError:
                chunk = ""
            for l in chunk.splitlines():
                try:
                    r = json.loads(l)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                ids = ", ".join(f"#{i}" for i in r["ids"][-3:])
                o, n = r["outcome"], r["name"]
                if o == "slept":
                    emit(col("2", f"{n}: nothing to add ({ids})"))
                elif o == "held":
                    emit(col("2", f"{n} answered ({r['note']}; held until all are in)"))
                elif o == "failed":
                    emit(col("31", f"{n} failed on {ids}: {r['note']}"))
                elif o == "gave up":
                    emit(col("31", f"{n} gave up on {ids} {r['note']}; those messages are skipped"))
                elif o == "budget":
                    emit(col("33", f"budget reached ({r['note']} since you spoke): agents wait for your next message"))
                elif o == "revealed":
                    emit(col("35", f"◆ independent round {ids} revealed: {r['note']}"))
            zz = {n: tuple((asleep(n) or {}).get("from") or ()) for n in AGENTS
                  if asleep(n) and n not in state["busy"]}  # who sleeps, and on whom (a woken agent at work is awake)
            if zz != state.setdefault("zz", zz):
                if not tty:   # in a terminal the status line above the prompt shows this in place
                    woke = sorted(set(state["zz"]) - set(zz))
                    emit((f"{', '.join(woke)} awake; " if woke else "") + sleep_summary(set(zz)))
                state["zz"] = zz
            if not tty and list(state["busy"]) != state.get("said"):
                state["said"] = list(state["busy"])
                if state["busy"]:
                    emit("… " + "; ".join(f"{n} {act_text(a)}" for n, a in state["busy"].items()))
            time.sleep(0.5)

    print(col("2", "Live chat. Type a message and press Enter to post it. @name,name at the start addresses it "
                   "(sticky); @name inside a message pings a sleeping agent; /to NAME sets recipients; /sleep NAME [30m] [until NAME], "
                   "/wake NAME; /audit or /design TEXT asks for a longer structured answer; /independent TEXT (/ind) has every "
                   "agent answer blind, revealed together; /decide TEXT records a decision, /decisions lists them; /last N shows the last N messages, /all the whole thread; "
                   "/status; /quit or Ctrl-D leaves."))
    if not tty and any(asleep(n) for n in AGENTS):
        print(sleep_summary({n for n in AGENTS if asleep(n)}))
    if after is not None:
        for m in load():
            if m["id"] > after:
                show(m)
                state["last"] = m["id"]
        after = None
    threading.Thread(target=follow, daemon=True).start()
    threading.Thread(target=animate, daemon=True).start()
    def reading():  # readline has drawn its prompt and waits for keys: from now on redraws must redraw the prompt
        with lock:
            state["reading"] = True
    readline.set_pre_input_hook(reading)
    while True:
        try:
            line = input(rl_prompt())
        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):
            with lock:
                if tty:   # clear the status line and whatever was typed
                    sys.stdout.write("\r" + mv(up() + (1 if state["shown"] else 0)) + "\033[J")
                state["reading"] = False
                state["stop"] = True
            print()
            break
        with lock:
            state["reading"] = False   # until the next input() draws its own prompt
        cols = shutil.get_terminal_size().columns
        vis = vwidth(plain_prompt()) + vwidth(line)
        echo_rows = max(1, -(-vis // cols))   # rows your typed line takes = rows from its first row to the cursor
        with lock:  # Enter left the status line above your line: clear both, redraw your line in its place
            if state["shown"] and tty:
                sys.stdout.write(f"\033[{echo_rows + 1}A\r\033[J" + prompt() + hl_input(line) + "\r\n")
                sys.stdout.flush()
                state["shown"] = False
        line = line.strip()
        if not line:
            continue
        if line in ("/q", "/quit", "/exit"):
            with lock:
                state["stop"] = True
            break
        if line == "/all" or line.startswith("/last"):
            n = line[5:].strip()
            msgs = load()
            for m in (msgs if line == "/all" else msgs[-(int(n) if n.isdigit() else 20):]):
                show(m)
            continue
        if line == "/status":
            emit(subprocess.run([sys.executable, SCRIPT, "--dir", WS, "status"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.rstrip())
            continue
        if line.startswith(("/sleep", "/wake")):
            cmd, *rest = line[1:].split()
            for n in (rest[:1] or [""])[0].split(","):
                if n not in AGENTS:
                    emit(col("31", f"usage: /{cmd} NAME[,NAME] [30m] [until NAME]; agents: {', '.join(AGENTS)}"))
                    break
                wf = rest[rest.index("until") + 1].split(",") if "until" in rest[:-1] else []
                dur = [x for x in rest[1:] if x != "until" and x not in wf]
                try:
                    sleep_set(n, cmd == "sleep", parse_dur(dur[0]) if cmd == "sleep" and dur else None, "user", wf)
                except ValueError:
                    emit(col("31", f"bad duration {rest[1]!r}; e.g. 30m, 2h"))
            continue
        if line.startswith("/to"):
            state["to"] = line[3:].strip() or "all"
            continue
        if line == "/decisions":
            emit(decisions_text(load()).rstrip() or "no decisions recorded yet (/decide TEXT records one)")
            continue
        mode = None
        mm = re.match(r"/(independent|ind|audit|design|decide)\b\s*(.*)", line, re.S)
        if mm:
            mode, line = {"ind": "independent", "decide": "decision"}.get(mm.group(1), mm.group(1)), mm.group(2).strip()
            if not line:
                emit(col("31", f"usage: /{mm.group(1)} TEXT"))
                continue
        if line.startswith("@"):
            tgt, _, rest = line[1:].partition(" ")
            state["to"] = tgt
            if tgt.lower() != "all":   # a leading @all stays in the text: it asks everyone (no lead turn)
                line = rest.strip()
            elif not rest.strip():
                continue
            if not line:
                continue
        try:
            m = post("user", "all" if mode == "decision" else state["to"], line, mode=mode)
        except SystemExit as e:
            emit(col("31", str(e)))
            continue
        seen("user", max(seen("user"), m["id"]))
        with lock:
            fresh = state["last"] == m["id"] - 1   # nothing arrived in between, so your line is right above
            state["last"] = max(state["last"], m["id"])
        if tty and fresh:   # swap your typed line for the numbered message
            with lock:
                sys.stdout.write(f"\033[{echo_rows}A\r\033[J")
            show(m)
        else:
            state["mine"].add(m["id"])
            emit(col("2", f"posted #{m['id']}"))
    state["stop"] = True


VOTE_ASK = ("Pick one of: {opts}. Say why in a few lines, and end with a line `VOTE: <option>`; or `VOTE: abstain`, "
            "or `VOTE: insufficient evidence` if the code can't settle it (then say what would).")
VOTE = re.compile(r"^\W*VOTE:\s*(.+?)\W*$", re.I | re.M)
SPECIAL = ("abstain", "insufficient evidence")


def discussion(q, msgs):
    """Ids of q and every message answering it, directly or down a reply chain (the `re` links)."""
    ids = {q["id"]}
    for m in msgs:
        if m["id"] > q["id"] and set(m.get("re") or ()) & ids:
            ids.add(m["id"])
    return ids


def settle(q, timeout, show=print):
    """Stream the messages after question q (a message dict) until it is answered: every served agent expected to
    take it up has had a turn on its discussion (q and the replies to it: posted, had nothing to add, or failed for
    good) and none of the discussion is waiting for an agent (checked twice). Work on other topics doesn't hold it
    up. Ends early when the discussion goes quiet for 2 min with turns missing, and at timeout. Returns
    (messages, outcomes {agent: [str]}, reason, status) with status "answered", "incomplete" or "timeout"."""
    t0, shown, calm, quiet = time.time(), q["id"] - 1, 0, None
    expect = [n for n in AUTO if pinged(q, n) or "all" in q["to"] and (asleep(n) or {}).get("why") != "user"]
    while True:
        msgs = load()
        for m in msgs:
            if m["id"] > shown:
                if m["id"] > q["id"]:
                    show(fmt(m))
                shown = m["id"]
        disc = discussion(q, msgs)
        rows = [r for r in turns_since(t0 - 5) if set(r["ids"]) & disc]
        done = {r["name"] for r in rows if r["outcome"] in ("posted", "slept", "held", "gave up")}
        # an agent's messages stay unread until its reply is posted, so this also covers turns in progress
        live = [n for n in AUTO if any(m["id"] in disc and m["id"] > seen(n) and for_me(m, n) for m in msgs)]
        held = [r for r in open_rounds() if r in disc]
        calm = 0 if live or held else calm + 1
        missing = [n for n in expect if n not in done]
        reason, status = None, None
        if calm >= 2 and not missing:
            reason, status = "answered: every agent asked had its turn and nothing is pending", "answered"
        elif calm >= 2:
            quiet = quiet or time.time()
            if time.time() - quiet > 120:
                reason, status = f"incomplete: quiet for 2 min without a turn from {', '.join(missing)}", "incomplete"
        else:
            quiet = None
        if not reason and time.time() - t0 > timeout:
            reason, status = f"timed out after {timeout:.0f}s; still working: {', '.join(live) or 'none'}", "timeout"
        if reason:
            outcomes = {}
            for r in rows:
                if r["name"] in AGENTS:
                    outcomes.setdefault(r["name"], []).append(
                        f"#{r['msg']}" if r["outcome"] == "posted" else "nothing to add" if r["outcome"] == "slept"
                        else r["outcome"] + (f" ({r['note']})" if r.get("note") else ""))
            for n in expect:
                outcomes.setdefault(n, ["no turn"])
            return [m for m in msgs if m["id"] > q["id"]], outcomes, reason, status
        time.sleep(2)


def vkey(v):
    """A vote or option compared by its words and symbols, ignoring case, spacing and surrounding quotes/marks."""
    return " ".join(v.strip().strip("`*_\"'.,:;!").lower().split())


def norm_vote(v, options):
    """The option (or abstain / insufficient evidence) a VOTE line names, else None."""
    k = vkey(v)
    return next((o for o in tuple(options) + SPECIAL if vkey(o) == k), None)


def tally(msgs, options):
    """{agent: (vote, message)} from each agent's latest VOTE line (a later invalid vote cancels an earlier valid
    one), and {agent: invalid text}."""
    votes, bad = {}, {}
    for m in msgs:
        v = VOTE.findall(m["text"]) if m["from"] in AGENTS else []
        if v:
            pick = norm_vote(v[-1], options)
            if pick:
                votes[m["from"]] = (pick, m)
                bad.pop(m["from"], None)
            else:
                bad[m["from"]] = v[-1].strip()
                votes.pop(m["from"], None)
    return votes, bad


def why(m):
    """An agent's reason for its vote: its message without the VOTE line, in one line."""
    return clip(" ".join(VOTE.sub("", m["text"]).split()), 300)


def verdict(votes, voters, final):
    """(label, option, exit code) for a tally, or None to vote again. Consensus: every voter voted, all for one
    option (abstentions allowed). After the last round: majority (over half of the voters for one option),
    insufficient evidence (over half say so), else no consensus."""
    picks = {n: v for n, (v, _) in votes.items()}
    real = {n: v for n, v in picks.items() if v != "abstain"}
    if set(picks) >= set(voters) and len(set(real.values())) == 1 and "insufficient evidence" not in real.values():
        return "CONSENSUS", next(iter(real.values())), 0
    if not final:
        return None
    for v in set(picks.values()) - {"abstain"}:
        if sum(1 for x in picks.values() if x == v) * 2 > len(voters):
            return ("INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE", v, 7) if v == "insufficient evidence" else ("MAJORITY", v, 6)
    return "NO CONSENSUS", None, 4


def converse(via, to, text, options=None, rounds=1, timeout=1800.0, mode=None):
    """An agent speaking for the user: post as the user, then follow the discussion it starts until the question
    is answered (see settle), and print who answered and why it stopped. With options it's a vote of every agent,
    re-asked up to `rounds` times until unanimous; agents that gave no valid vote are asked once more within the
    round. Exit code: 0 settled (vote: consensus), 3 timed out, 4 no consensus, 5 incomplete (an agent asked
    never took its turn), 6 majority, 7 insufficient evidence."""
    ensure_serve()
    if not AUTO:
        print("note: no agents are run by `agora serve` here; nothing will answer automatically", file=sys.stderr)
    if options:
        keys = [vkey(o) for o in options]
        if len(set(keys)) < len(keys) or set(keys) & set(SPECIAL) or not all(keys):
            print(f"ambiguous or reserved vote options {options}: they must differ beyond case and spacing, and "
                  f"not be {' or '.join(SPECIAL)}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        to = ",".join(AGENTS)   # named explicitly: everyone votes, sleepers included, no lead-answer turns
    vote = VOTE_ASK.format(opts=", ".join(options)) if options else ""
    body = text.strip() + ("\n\n" + vote if vote else "")

    def follow(q):
        print(f"posted #{q['id']} as user via {via}; following the discussion…", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        new, outcomes, reason, status = settle(q, timeout)
        print(f"\nSETTLED: {reason}")
        for n, o in sorted(outcomes.items()):
            print(f"  {n}: {', '.join(o)}")
        return new, status

    for rnd in range(1, rounds + 1):
        q = post("user", to, body, via=via, mode=mode)
        new, status = follow(q)
        if status == "timeout":
            return 3
        if not options:
            return 0 if status == "answered" else 5
        votes, bad = tally(new, options)
        redo = [n for n in AUTO if n not in votes]
        if redo:   # one more chance within the round for agents with no valid vote
            nq = post("user", ",".join(redo), " ".join("@" + n for n in redo) + ": you gave no valid vote on #"
                      f"{q['id']}. Reply with your vote now, choosing exactly one of: {', '.join(options)} (or "
                      "abstain / insufficient evidence), as a last line `VOTE: <option>`.", via=via, re_=[q["id"]])
            more, status = follow(nq)
            if status == "timeout":
                return 3
            votes, bad = tally(new + more, options)
        absent = [n for n in AUTO if n not in votes and n not in bad]
        print("votes: " + (", ".join(f"{n} {v}" for n, (v, _) in votes.items()) or "none")
              + (f"; invalid: {', '.join(f'{n} {v!r}' for n, v in bad.items())}" if bad else "")
              + (f"; no vote: {', '.join(absent)}" if absent else ""))
        res = verdict(votes, AUTO, rnd == rounds)
        if res:
            label, pick, code = res
            print(f"{label}" + (f": {pick}" if pick and label != "INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE" else ""))
            for n, (v, m) in votes.items():
                if label != "NO CONSENSUS" and v != pick:
                    print(f"  minority {n} ({v}, #{m['id']}): {why(m)}")
            if pick:
                post("user", "all", f"Vote on #{q['id']}: {label.lower()}"
                     + (f" for {pick}" if label != "INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE" else "") + " ("
                     + ", ".join(f"{n} {v}" for n, (v, _) in votes.items()) + ").", via=via, mode="decision",
                     re_=[q["id"]])
            return code
        body = (f"Round {rnd + 1}: no consensus yet on #{q['id']} (" + (", ".join(f"{n}: {v}" for n, (v, _) in
                votes.items()) or "no valid votes") + ")."
                + " Read the others' reasons above, answer the strongest one you disagree with, and vote again. "
                + vote)


def parse_dur(d):
    if not d:
        return None
    mult = {"s": 1, "m": 60, "h": 3600}.get(d[-1].lower())
    return float(d[:-1]) * mult if mult else float(d) * 60


def where():
    print(f"workspace  {WS}" + ("  (legacy: in the install dir)" if WS == INSTALL else ""))
    print(f"source     {SRC or '(none: a discussion without code)'}"
          + ("" if not SRC else "  (git repo)" if git_top(SRC) else "  (plain folder)"))
    print(f"install    {INSTALL}")
    print(f"config     {CONFIG}" + ("" if WS == INSTALL else f" over {ICONFIG}"))
    print(f"thread     {MD}")


def list_ws():
    rows = [(INSTALL, _json(ICONFIG).get("src"))] if _json(ICONFIG).get("src") else []
    if os.path.isdir(DATA):
        rows += [(os.path.join(DATA, d), _json(os.path.join(DATA, d, "workspace.json")).get("src"))
                 for d in sorted(os.listdir(DATA)) if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(DATA, d, "workspace.json"))]
    for d, src in rows:
        t = os.path.join(d, "thread.jsonl")
        n = sum(1 for _ in open(t)) if os.path.exists(t) else 0
        when = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M", time.localtime(os.path.getmtime(t))) if n else "-"
        print(f"{'*' if d == WS else ' '} {os.path.basename(d):40s} {n:5d} msgs  last {when}  {src or '(no source)'}")


def ask(q, default=""):
    try:
        r = input(f"{q} " + (f"[{default}] " if default and not q.endswith("]") else "")).strip()
    except EOFError:
        print()
        return default
    return r or default


def pick(title, options, current):
    """Numbered choice from options [(value, note)]; Enter keeps current, or type any value."""
    print(f"\n{title}" + (f" (now: {current})" if current else ""))
    for i, (v, note) in enumerate(options, 1):
        print(f"  {i:2d}. {v}" + (f"  {note}" if note else ""))
    r = ask("  number or name, Enter keeps it:")
    if r.isdigit() and 1 <= int(r) <= len(options):
        return options[int(r) - 1][0]
    return r or current


def cli_models(name):
    """[(model, note)] the CLI offers, best effort ([] when it can't say), and {model: [efforts]}."""
    try:
        if name == "codex":
            r = subprocess.run(["codex", "debug", "models"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60,
                               env=agent_env("codex"))
            ms = [m for m in json.loads(r.stdout).get("models", []) if m.get("visibility") == "list"]
            return ([(m["slug"], m.get("description", "")) for m in ms],
                    {m["slug"]: [e["effort"] for e in m.get("supported_reasoning_levels", [])] for m in ms})
        if name == "gemini":
            r = subprocess.run([AGY, "models"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
            return [tuple((l.split("\t") + [""])[:2]) for l in r.stdout.splitlines() if "\t" in l], {}
        h = subprocess.run([CLAUDE, "--help"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60).stdout
        m, e = re.search(r"--model <model>(.*?)\n  -", h, re.S), re.search(r"--effort <level>.*?\((.*?)\)", h, re.S)
        return ([(x, "") for x in re.findall(r"'([\w.-]+)'", m.group(1))] if m else [],
                {"*": [x.strip() for x in e.group(1).split(",")]} if e else {})
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return [], {}


def save_cfg(path, upd):
    cfg = _json(path)
    cfg.update(upd)
    for k in [k for k, v in cfg.items() if v in ("", None)]:
        del cfg[k]
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
        json.dump(cfg, f, indent=2)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)


def setup():
    """Interactive: what to leave out of the snapshot, which agents to seat, their models and efforts."""
    where()
    if SRC:   # 1. excludes, with the biggest top-level entries and the usual suspects suggested
        print("\nScanning the source…")
        sizes, counts = {}, {}
        for f in list_files(SRC):
            if excluded(f, SECRETS):
                continue
            top = f.split("/")[0] + ("/" if "/" in f else "")
            try:
                sizes[top] = sizes.get(top, 0) + os.path.getsize(os.path.join(SRC, f))
                counts[top] = counts.get(top, 0) + 1
            except OSError:
                pass
        usual = {"data/", "runs/", "logs/", "log/", "node_modules/", "dist/", "build/", "out/", "outputs/", "tmp/",
                 "checkpoints/", "models/", "wandb/", "venv/", ".venv/", "target/", "vendor/", "__pycache__/"}
        cur = list(EXCLUDE)
        sugg = [t for t in sizes if t not in cur and (t in usual or sizes[t] > 50 * 2**20)]
        print(f"{sum(counts.values())} files, {sum(sizes.values()) / 2**20:.1f} MB. Largest:")
        for t in sorted(sizes, key=sizes.get, reverse=True)[:12]:
            print(f"  {t:30s} {sizes[t] / 2**20:8.1f} MB {counts[t]:6d} files" + ("  (suggested)" if t in sugg else "")
                  + ("  (excluded)" if t in cur else ""))
        print(f"Excluded now: {', '.join(cur) or 'nothing'} (secrets like .env*, *.pem, *.key always are)")
        r = ask("Exclude (space-separated paths or globs; Enter = now + suggested, - = clear):",
                " ".join(cur + sugg))
        save_cfg(CONFIG, {"exclude": [] if r == "-" else r.split()})
    found = [n for n in AGENTS if shutil.which({"claude": CLAUDE, "codex": "codex", "gemini": AGY}[n])]
    print(f"\nAgent CLIs found: {', '.join(found) or 'none'}")
    seat = ask("Which agents should answer automatically (space-separated)?", " ".join(n for n in AUTO if n in found)
               or " ".join(found)).split()
    inst = {"serve": [n for n in seat if n in AGENTS]}
    for n in inst["serve"]:
        models, efforts = cli_models(n)
        cur = opt(n, "model") or ""
        inst[f"{n}_model"] = pick(f"{n} model", models, cur) if models else ask(f"\n{n} model (Enter: CLI default):", cur)
        effs = efforts.get(inst[f"{n}_model"]) or efforts.get("*")
        if effs:
            inst[f"{n}_effort"] = pick(f"{n} effort", [(e, "") for e in effs], opt(n, "effort") or "")
    if WS == INSTALL or ask("\nUse these agents and models for all workspaces? [Y/n]", "y").lower().startswith("y"):
        save_cfg(ICONFIG, inst)
    else:
        save_cfg(CONFIG, inst)
    if "codex" in inst["serve"] and not os.path.exists(os.path.join(INSTALL, ".codex-home", "auth.json")):
        print(f"\nLog Codex in once (agora's own Codex home): CODEX_HOME={os.path.join(INSTALL, '.codex-home')} codex login")
    try:
        import rich  # noqa: F401
    except ImportError:
        if ask("\nInstall rich (markdown in the chat) into agora's own .venv? [y/N]", "n").lower().startswith("y"):
            subprocess.run([sys.executable, "-m", "venv", VENV], check=True)
            subprocess.run([os.path.join(VENV, "bin", "pip"), "install", "-q", "-r",
                            os.path.join(INSTALL, "requirements.txt")], check=True)
    print("\nSaved. `agora` joins the chat; `agora sync` refreshes the snapshot.")


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument("--dir", help="the workspace dir to use (default: the one for this folder; env AGORA_DIR)")
    ap.add_argument("--src", help="the folder to discuss (default: this git repo, else this folder)")
    ap.add_argument("--no-src", action="store_true", help="a discussion without code")
    ap.add_argument("--last", type=int, help="with no command: join the chat showing this many earlier messages (default 20)")
    sp = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")
    p = sp.add_parser("post"); p.add_argument("-a", "--as", dest="who")
    p.add_argument("--via", metavar="AGENT", help="an agent posting as the user: follows the discussion it starts "
                   "and prints it, returning once the agents have settled")
    p.add_argument("--vote", metavar="A,B", help="with --via: every agent votes between these options")
    p.add_argument("--rounds", type=int, default=1, help="with --vote: re-ask up to N rounds until unanimous")
    p.add_argument("--timeout", type=float, default=1800, help="with --via: give up after this many seconds")
    p.add_argument("-t", "--to", default="all"); p.add_argument("-f", "--file"); p.add_argument("text", nargs="*")
    p.add_argument("-q", "--no-follow", action="store_true", help="just post; don't open the live chat")
    p.add_argument("--mode", choices=MODES, help="reply shape: short (default), audit or design (longer, structured "
                   "findings), independent (every agent answers blind; the answers are revealed together, then "
                   "cross-checked)")
    p.add_argument("--independent", dest="mode", action="store_const", const="independent", help="= --mode independent")
    p = sp.add_parser("chat"); p.add_argument("-t", "--to", default="all")
    p.add_argument("--last", type=int, default=20, help="show this many earlier messages on joining")
    p = sp.add_parser("read"); p.add_argument("-a", "--as", dest="who"); p.add_argument("--new", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--last", type=int); p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p = sp.add_parser("wait"); p.add_argument("-a", "--as", dest="who", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--timeout", type=float, default=0)
    p.add_argument("--until", help="block until this participant (e.g. codex) posts, or you are pinged")
    p = sp.add_parser("skill", help="print the agent skill (SKILL.md) with this agora's paths, or install it")
    p.add_argument("--install", metavar="DIR", help="write DIR/agora/SKILL.md (e.g. ~/.claude/skills)")
    p = sp.add_parser("idle"); p.add_argument("-a", "--as", dest="who", required=True)
    p = sp.add_parser("doing"); p.add_argument("-a", "--as", dest="who", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--id", help="a concurrent action (several may run at once); without --id TEXT sets the phase")
    p.add_argument("--bg", action="store_true", help="the action runs in the background")
    p.add_argument("--done", action="store_true", help="the action with --id finished")
    p.add_argument("text", nargs="*")
    p = sp.add_parser("sleep", help="stop answering messages to all until pinged (@name or -t name)")
    p.add_argument("-a", "--as", dest="who", required=True); p.add_argument("--for", dest="dur", help="e.g. 30m, 2h")
    p.add_argument("--until", help="also wake when this participant (e.g. codex) posts next")
    p.add_argument("--via", metavar="AGENT", help="put another agent to sleep for the user, like /sleep in the chat")
    p.add_argument("why", nargs="*")
    p = sp.add_parser("wake"); p.add_argument("-a", "--as", dest="who", required=True)
    p = sp.add_parser("hook", help="Claude Code tool hook (reads hook JSON on stdin)"); p.add_argument("phase", choices=["pre", "post"])
    sp.add_parser("protocol"); p = sp.add_parser("intro", help="the starter prompt for a seat you run by hand")
    p.add_argument("name", choices=AGENTS)
    p = sp.add_parser("decide", help="record a decision (shown at the top of the thread; nobody is asked to reply)")
    p.add_argument("--via", metavar="AGENT", help="an agent recording it for the user"); p.add_argument("text", nargs="+")
    sp.add_parser("decisions", help="list the recorded decisions")
    sp.add_parser("sync"); sp.add_parser("status")
    sp.add_parser("setup", help="choose excludes, the agents to seat, and their models and efforts")
    sp.add_parser("where", help="this folder's workspace, source and config")
    sp.add_parser("ls", help="list the workspaces")
    for n in AGENTS:
        sp.add_parser(n, help=f"run {n} once headlessly on the thread")
    p = sp.add_parser("reset", help="drop agent sessions; their next turn starts fresh"); p.add_argument("name", nargs="?", default="all")
    p = sp.add_parser("serve"); p.add_argument("--budget", type=int, default=BUDGET)
    p.add_argument("--only", help="comma list of agents to serve (default: config serve, else all)")
    p.add_argument("--auto", action="store_true", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)   # started by a client: exits when idle
    a = ap.parse_args()

    if a.cmd == "setup":
        return setup()
    if a.cmd == "where":
        return where()
    if a.cmd == "ls":
        return list_ws()
    if WS_HOW == "new" and a.cmd in (None, "chat") and sys.stdin.isatty():
        print(f"New agora workspace for {SRC or 'a discussion without code'} (data in {WS}).")
        if ask("Run setup now (excludes, agents, models)? [Y/n]", "y").lower().startswith("y"):
            setup()
    if a.cmd in (None, "chat"):
        msgs = load()
        last = a.last if a.last is not None else 20
        return chat(getattr(a, "to", "all"), after=msgs[-min(last, len(msgs))]["id"] - 1 if msgs and last else None)
    if a.cmd == "post" and a.via:
        if a.who and a.who.lower() != "user":
            sys.exit("--via posts as the user; drop -a")
        text = (open(a.file).read() if a.file else sys.stdin.read() if a.text == ["-"] or not a.text
                else " ".join(a.text))
        if not text.strip():
            sys.exit("empty message")
        sys.exit(converse(a.via.lower(), a.to, text, [o.strip() for o in a.vote.split(",")] if a.vote else None,
                          max(1, a.rounds), a.timeout, a.mode))
    if a.cmd == "post":
        if a.vote:
            sys.exit("--vote needs --via AGENT")
        if not a.who:
            sys.exit("post needs -a NAME (or --via AGENT to post as the user)")
        live = a.who.lower() == "user" and not a.no_follow and sys.stdin.isatty() and sys.stdout.isatty()
        if live and not a.text and not a.file:
            return chat(a.to)
        text = (open(a.file).read() if a.file else sys.stdin.read() if a.text == ["-"] or not a.text
                else " ".join(a.text))
        if a.mode and a.who.lower() != "user":
            sys.exit("--mode is for the user's messages")
        client()   # an idle serve can't exit between this post and the check below
        who, msgs = a.who.lower(), load()
        asked = [q for q in open_rounds() if any(m["id"] == q and pinged(m, who) for m in msgs)]
        m = post(a.who, a.to, text, mode=a.mode, hold=asked)
        if not m.get("held") and any(for_me(m, x) for x in AUTO):
            ensure_serve()
        if m.get("held"):
            print(f"held: independent round #{m['held']} is open; your answer is revealed with the others'")
            return
        if a.who.lower() in NAMES:
            seen(a.who.lower(), max(seen(a.who.lower()), m["id"]))
        print(f"posted #{m['id']}")
        if live:
            chat(a.to, after=m["id"] - 1)
    elif a.cmd == "read":
        msgs = load()
        if a.new:
            if not a.who:
                sys.exit("--new needs -a NAME")
            msgs = [m for m in msgs if for_me(m, a.who) and m["id"] > seen(a.who)]
            if msgs:
                seen(a.who, msgs[-1]["id"])
        if a.last:
            msgs = msgs[-a.last:]
        print("\n".join(json.dumps(m, ensure_ascii=False) for m in msgs) if a.json else "\n".join(fmt(m) for m in msgs))
    elif a.cmd == "wait":
        t0 = time.time()
        ensure_serve()   # a waiting seat is a client: the serve stays up while it waits
        if a.until:
            sleep_set(a.who, True, why="waiting for " + a.until, until_from=a.until.lower().split(","))
        while True:
            msgs, last = load(), seen(a.who)
            if any(for_me(m, a.who) and m["id"] > last for m in msgs):
                new = [m for m in msgs if m["id"] > last and m["from"] != a.who]  # everything, not just yours
                seen(a.who, msgs[-1]["id"])
                sleep_set(a.who, False)
                if a.who != "user":
                    busy(a.who, True, "reading the new messages")
                print("\n".join(fmt(m) for m in new))
                return
            if a.timeout and time.time() - t0 > a.timeout:
                sys.exit(3)
            time.sleep(2)
    elif a.cmd == "skill":
        s = template(os.path.join("skills", "agora", "SKILL.md"), agora=SCRIPT)
        if not a.install:
            print(s, end="")
        else:
            d = os.path.join(os.path.expanduser(a.install), "agora")
            os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
            with open(os.path.join(d, "SKILL.md"), "w") as f:
                f.write(s)
            print(f"wrote {os.path.join(d, 'SKILL.md')}")
    elif a.cmd == "idle":
        busy(a.who.lower(), False)
    elif a.cmd == "doing":
        if a.id:
            act(a.who.lower(), a.id, None if a.done else (" ".join(a.text) or "working"), bg=a.bg)
        else:
            busy(a.who.lower(), True, " ".join(a.text) or "thinking")
    elif a.cmd == "sleep":
        wf = a.until.lower().split(",") if a.until else []
        sleep_set(a.who.lower(), True, parse_dur(a.dur), "user" if a.via else " ".join(a.why), wf)
        print(f"{a.who} sleeps until pinged" + (f" or {a.until} posts" if wf else "") + (f" or {a.dur} pass" if a.dur else ""))
    elif a.cmd == "wake":
        sleep_set(a.who.lower(), False)
    elif a.cmd == "hook":
        claude_hook(a.phase)
    elif a.cmd == "protocol":
        print(protocol())
    elif a.cmd == "intro":
        code, pre = winpath(CODE)
        print(template("SEAT.md", name=a.name, others=",".join(n for n in AGENTS if n != a.name), code=code,
                       cmd=pre + AGORA))
    elif a.cmd == "decide":
        client()
        m = post("user", "all", " ".join(a.text), via=a.via and a.via.lower(), mode="decision")
        print(f"recorded decision #{m['id']}")
    elif a.cmd == "decisions":
        print(decisions_text(load()).rstrip() or "no decisions recorded yet")
    elif a.cmd == "sync":
        n = sync()
        if n is not None:
            print(f"synced {n} files to {CODE}")
    elif a.cmd in AGENTS:
        m = run_agent(a.cmd)
        print("slept" if m == "slept" else f"held for independent round #{m['held']}" if m and m.get("held")
              else f"posted #{m['id']}" if m else "no reply")
    elif a.cmd == "serve":
        import threading
        who = [x for x in (a.only.split(",") if a.only else AUTO)]
        held = serve_lock()   # one serve per workspace (kept open for the life of the process)
        if held is None:
            sys.exit(0 if a.auto else "agora serve is already running (see state/serve.lock)")
        if not a.auto:   # auto-started serves reuse these
            serve_policy(a.only, a.budget if a.budget != BUDGET else None, save=True)
        idle_after = float(CFG.get("idle_exit", 1800)) if a.auto else 0   # seconds; 0: never
        last_busy = time.time()

        def quiet(msgs):
            """Nothing to do now or soon: no agent working or with unread messages (unless over budget), no
            retry due, no open independent round, no sleep that ends by itself."""
            over = agent_streak(msgs) >= a.budget
            return not working and not open_rounds() and not any(
                (not over and any(m["id"] > seen(n) and for_me(m, n) for m in msgs))
                or failure(n) or (asleep(n) or {}).get("until") for n in who)
        print(f"serving {who} in parallel (budget {a.budget} agent msgs per user msg); Ctrl-C to stop", flush=True)
        working, wlock = set(), threading.Lock()

        def turn(name, ids):
            try:
                m = run_agent(name, do_sync=False, served=True)
                print(f"{time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')} {name} -> " + ("asleep" if m == "slept" else
                      "nothing new" if m == "nothing" else
                      f"held for round #{m['held']}" if m and m.get("held") else
                      f"#{m['id']}" if m else "failed"), flush=True)
            except Exception as e:  # keep serving the others; the messages stay unseen and are retried
                f = note_failure(name, ids, None)
                log_turn(name, ids, "failed", note=f"error {e!r}, try {f['tries']}/{MAX_TRIES}")
                print(f"{name} -> error {e!r}", flush=True)
            finally:
                busy(name, False)
                with wlock:
                    working.discard(name)

        halted = os.path.join(STATE, "halted")   # present while the budget stops the agents (the chat shows it)
        if os.path.exists(halted):   # left over from an earlier serve: recomputed below
            os.unlink(halted)
        while True:
            reveal_due()
            msgs = load()
            todo = []
            over = agent_streak(msgs) >= a.budget
            if over != os.path.exists(halted):
                if over:
                    open(halted, "w").write(str(a.budget))
                    print(f"budget reached ({a.budget} agent msgs since the user spoke); waiting for the user",
                          flush=True)
                    log_turn("serve", [msgs[-1]["id"]], "budget", note=f"{a.budget} agent messages")
                else:
                    os.unlink(halted)
            for name in who:
                if name in working:
                    continue
                pend = [m for m in msgs if m["id"] > seen(name) and for_me(m, name)]
                if not pend or over:   # over budget: the messages stay unseen until the user speaks
                    continue
                f = failure(name)
                if f and f["tries"] >= MAX_TRIES:   # give up on these messages, visibly
                    give_up(name, f)
                    print(f"{name}: gave up on {f['ids']} after {f['tries']} failed tries", flush=True)
                    continue
                if f and time.time() < f["next"]:
                    continue
                todo.append((name, pend))
            if todo:
                with wlock:
                    idle = not working
                if idle:  # refresh the code snapshot only when no agent is reading it
                    sync()
                for name, pend in todo:
                    print(f"{time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')} {name} replying to {[m['id'] for m in pend]}", flush=True)
                    busy(name, True)
                    with wlock:
                        working.add(name)
                    threading.Thread(target=turn, args=(name, [m["id"] for m in pend]), daemon=True).start()
            if idle_after:
                with wlock:
                    q = quiet(msgs)
                if not q:
                    last_busy = time.time()
                elif time.time() - last_busy > idle_after:
                    cl = lockfile("clients.lock")
                    if lock(cl, block=False):   # no client is attached, and none can attach until we're gone
                        with wlock:
                            q = quiet(load())
                        if q:
                            print(f"{time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')} idle for {idle_after:.0f}s with no client; exiting",
                                  flush=True)
                            held.close()   # serve lock first: a client that gets in next starts a new serve
                            cl.close()
                            return
                    cl.close()
            time.sleep(2)
    elif a.cmd == "reset":
        for n in (AGENTS if a.name == "all" else [a.name]):
            if session(n):
                session(n, drop=True)
                print(f"{n}: session dropped; next turn starts fresh")
    elif a.cmd == "status":
        msgs = load()
        print(f"{len(msgs)} messages; agent streak {agent_streak(msgs)}; code snapshot: "
              + (open(os.path.join(CODE, 'SNAPSHOT.txt')).read().strip() if os.path.exists(CODE) else "none"))
        for n in NAMES:
            z = asleep(n)
            print(f"  {n:8s} seen #{seen(n)}, unread {sum(1 for m in msgs if for_me(m, n) and m['id'] > seen(n))}"
                  + (", asleep until pinged" + (f" or {','.join(z['from'])} posts" if z.get("from") else "") + (time.strftime(" (or %H:%M)", time.localtime(z["until"])) if z["until"] else "")
                     if z else ""))
        for n in AGENTS:
            se = session(n)
            print(f"  {n:8s} " + (f"session {se['id'][:8]}…: {se.get('turns', 0)}/{MAX_TURNS} turns, "
                                  f"{se.get('tokens', 0) // 1000}k/{MAX_TOKENS // 1000}k tokens, since {se.get('started')}"
                                  if se else "no session (next turn starts fresh)") + (" [served]" if n in AUTO else ""))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
